import { setExInfo } from '../library/howto.js';
setExInfo(`
Press hombro mancuernas|Lower the dumbbells to ear height and press them up without clanking them together at the top: that way the deltoid never gets a break.|Seated on a bench set at 80-90° with your back supported, bring the dumbbells to the sides of your shoulders with your palms facing forward. Press up and slightly inward until your elbows are almost straight, then lower slowly until the dumbbells are at ear height.
Press militar barra|Squeeze your glutes and abs before you press: if you arch your lower back, the load shifts to your back.|Standing with your feet hip-width apart, grip the bar slightly wider than your shoulders and rest it on your upper chest. Press straight up, moving your face out of the way, bring your head under the bar once it clears your forehead, and lock out with your arms next to your ears. Lower under control to your collarbone.
Press Arnold|Rotate your wrists during the press, not at the end: the rotation should go along with the whole push.|Seated with your back supported, start with the dumbbells in front of your face and your palms toward you, like the top of a curl. As you press, open your elbows and rotate your palms until they face forward at the top; on the way down, reverse the rotation back to the starting position.
Press hombro máquina|Adjust the seat so the handles sit at shoulder height: if you start lower, you load the joint without getting any extra work.|Set the seat, sit with your back against the pad, and grab the handles with your elbows slightly in front of your body. Press up without fully locking your elbows and come back slowly until the handles reach shoulder height.
Press hombro unilateral|Put your free hand on your waist and don't let your torso lean to the opposite side as you press.|Standing or seated, hold a dumbbell next to your shoulder with your palm facing forward or neutral. Press up with your torso straight and your abs tight, without leaning, and lower under control. Finish all the reps on one side before switching.
Press landmine|Press up and forward following the arc of the bar, with your elbow slightly in front of your body.|Put one end of the bar in a landmine attachment or a corner and hold the other end with one hand at shoulder height. Standing or with one knee on the floor, extend your arm forward and up along the arc, brace your core so you don't rotate, and return slowly to your shoulder.
Press militar sentado con barra|Keep your back against the pad the whole way; if it comes off, the exercise turns into an incline press.|Sit on an upright bench under the bar, racked at forehead height. Unrack it with a grip slightly wider than your shoulders, lower it to your upper chest, and press in a straight line until your elbows are almost straight.
Press hombro en Smith|Set the bench so the bar comes down just in front of your nose, not over your head.|Put an upright bench inside the Smith machine and sit with your back supported. Unlock the bar with a grip slightly wider than your shoulders, lower it under control to your chin, and press until your elbows are almost straight; when you finish, lock it again by rotating your wrists.
Press hombro con kettlebell|Rest the bell on your forearm (rack position) and squeeze the handle hard so your wrist doesn't bend.|Bring the kettlebell to the rack position, with the bell on your forearm and your elbow close to your body. Squeeze your glutes and abs and press straight up, turning your palm slightly forward until your arm is straight; lower under control back to the rack.
Press hombro en polea|Position yourself so the cable pulls in line with your forearm: if it pulls sideways, the shoulder loses the load.|Set two pulleys low and sit or stand between them with the handles at shoulder height. Press up until your hands almost meet overhead and lower slowly, feeling the cable tension through the whole range.
Press hombro sentado agarre neutro|With your palms facing each other, your elbows travel slightly forward: it's the most comfortable option if your shoulders bother you.|Seated with your back supported, hold the dumbbells at shoulder height with your palms facing each other. Press up with your elbows in front of your body and the dumbbells parallel, and lower under control to chin height.
Press hombro con bandas|The band gets heavier the more it stretches: slow down at the end of the press so you don't lose control at the top.|Step on the band with one or both feet and bring the ends to shoulder height with your palms facing forward. Press up against the resistance, which grows as you go, until your arms are straight, and return slowly to your shoulders without letting the band drag you down.
Press hombro con pausa|Pause for two seconds at the bottom without relaxing your shoulders: the pause takes away the bounce and makes you start from a dead stop.|Seated with your back supported, lower the dumbbells to ear height and hold the position for two seconds with your shoulders under tension. From the pause, press hard until your elbows are almost straight and repeat the controlled descent.
Elevaciones laterales|Raise with your elbows slightly bent and lead with them, not with your hands, up to shoulder height.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand at your sides and your torso leaning slightly forward, raise your arms out to the sides until they're parallel to the floor. Lower over about two seconds without letting the dumbbells touch your thighs.
Elevaciones laterales en polea|Start with your hand in front of the opposite hip: the cable gives tension right at the bottom, where the dumbbell doesn't.|Set the pulley low and stand sideways to it, holding the handle in the far hand. With your elbow slightly bent, raise your arm out and up to shoulder height and return slowly, crossing in front of your body.
Elevaciones laterales inclinado|Leaning sideways on an incline bench, the arm starts more stretched and you work the bottom of the range.|Lie on your side on a bench set at 30-45°, with your side supported and a dumbbell in the top hand hanging in front of you. Raise it out until your arm is slightly above horizontal and lower under control into the stretch.
Elevaciones laterales en máquina|Keep your arms tight against the pads and push with your elbows, not with your hands.|Adjust the seat so the machine's pivot lines up with your shoulder and rest the outside of your arms on the pads. Raise to horizontal, pause briefly, and lower slowly without losing tension between reps.
Elevaciones laterales a una mano en polea|Hold on to the post and lean out a little: that way the arm rises without your torso swinging.|Standing sideways to the low pulley, hold the post with your near hand and lean your body a few degrees outward. With the far hand, raise the handle out to the side up to shoulder height and lower under control until it crosses in front of your hip.
Elevaciones laterales sentado|Seated, you can't help with your legs: if you need to swing your torso, lower the weight.|Sitting on the edge of a bench with your back straight and a dumbbell at each side, raise your arms out to the sides with your elbows slightly bent up to shoulder height. Pause briefly at the top and lower slowly.
Elevaciones laterales con banda|Adjust the resistance by stepping on the band closer to or farther from the ends: with little free band, the load shoots up at the top.|Step on the middle of the band and hold one end in each hand next to your thighs. Raise your arms out to the sides with your elbows slightly bent up to shoulder height and return slowly, resisting the pull.
Elevaciones laterales tumbado de lado|Lying on your side, the heaviest part comes at the start of the movement: there's no need to go past vertical.|Lie on your side on a flat bench or the floor with a dumbbell in your top hand resting in front of your thigh. Raise your arm toward the ceiling with your elbow slightly bent until it's almost vertical and lower slowly until it almost touches your leg.
Elevaciones laterales parciales|Work only the bottom half, without going past 45°, to build up tension where the deltoid is most stretched.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand, raise your arms out to the sides only halfway and come back down without resting. Keep a steady pace and stop when your technique starts to break down.
Pájaros mancuernas|Move the dumbbells out, not back, and keep your shoulders away from your ears.|Standing with your torso bent almost parallel to the floor and your back straight, let the dumbbells hang under your chest with your elbows slightly bent. Open them out to the sides up to shoulder height, squeezing the back of your shoulders, and lower slowly.
Face pull|Pull the rope toward your forehead, spreading your hands apart, and finish with your thumbs pointing back.|Set the pulley at face height with a rope and grab it with your palms down. Take a step back and pull toward your forehead, opening your elbows and spreading the ends, rotate your arms outward at the end, and return slowly with your arms straight.
Pájaros en máquina|Use a neutral grip on the handles and don't let the plates touch between reps.|Sit facing the pad of the reverse fly machine, with your chest supported and the handles at shoulder height. Sweep your arms back in an arc, with your elbows almost straight, until they're in line with your body, and return slowly.
Pájaros en polea|Cross the cables, with your right hand on the left pulley's cable, to start with the rear delt stretched.|Stand between two pulleys set at chest height, with no handles, and grab each cable with the opposite hand. With your arms almost straight, open them out and back until they form a T and cross them in front again under control.
Elevación Y|Raise your arms in a Y with your thumbs up and use light weight: the target is the lower traps, not moving big numbers.|Lie face down on a bench set at 30-45° with a light dumbbell in each hand. Raise your straight arms forward and out to form a Y, thumbs toward the ceiling, up to ear level, and lower slowly.
Pájaros en banco inclinado|With your chest supported on the bench, your lower back stays out of it: there's no way to cheat with momentum.|Lie face down on a bench set at about 30°, with your chest supported and the dumbbells hanging. Open them out to the sides with your elbows slightly bent up to shoulder height, squeeze for a second, and lower under control.
Face pull con banda|Anchor the band at eye level and spread your hands as you pull, as if you were hitting a double biceps pose.|Anchor the band at face height and hold one end in each hand. Step back until you feel tension and pull toward your face, opening your elbows and bringing your hands to the sides of your head; return slowly until your arms are straight.
Remo posterior con mancuernas|Keep your elbows flared, perpendicular to your torso: the high elbow is what puts the rear delt to work.|With your torso bent almost parallel to the floor and a dumbbell in each hand, row by driving your elbows out and up, with your arms perpendicular to your body, up to back level. Lower under control without dropping the weight.
Elevación T|Keep your arms out in a cross with your thumbs up and squeeze your shoulder blades together at the end of each rep.|Lie face down on an incline bench with a light dumbbell in each hand. Raise your straight arms out to the sides, forming a T with your body, up to the line of your back, squeeze your shoulder blades together for a second, and lower slowly.
Face pull a una mano|Do it one arm at a time to even out both sides, and rotate your torso as little as possible.|Set the pulley at face height with a single handle. Facing it or slightly sideways, pull with one hand toward your temple, opening your elbow out and rotating your arm at the end; return with your arm straight and switch sides when the set is done.
Press banca|Squeeze your shoulder blades together and keep them there for the whole set: your chest comes up and your shoulders stay protected.|Lie down with your eyes under the bar, feet planted on the floor, and shoulder blades squeezed together. Grip the bar slightly wider than your shoulders, unrack it, and lower it under control to your lower chest with your elbows about 45° from your body. Press up and slightly back until your arms are straight.
Press pecho máquina|Adjust the seat so the handles sit at mid-chest height, and don't let your back come off the pad.|Sit with your back supported and grab the handles with your wrists straight and your elbows slightly below your shoulders. Press forward until your arms are almost straight, without locking out, and return slowly until you feel the stretch in your chest.
Press banca mancuernas|Lower the dumbbells a little deeper than you would a bar: the extra range is this exercise's advantage.|Sit with a dumbbell in each hand on your thighs, kick them up as you lie back, and position them over your chest. Lower them with your elbows about 45° out until they're at chest height and press up, bringing them slightly together without letting them touch.
Press banca en Smith|Set the bench so the bar comes down over your lower chest: on the guide rails you can't correct the path.|Put a flat bench inside the Smith machine so the bar is over your chest. Unlock the bar with your shoulder blades squeezed together, lower it slowly until it grazes your chest, and press until your elbows are straight; lock it when you finish.
Press pecho máquina convergente|The handles come together as you press: squeeze your chest at the end as if you wanted to bring your hands together.|Adjust the seat so the handles come out at mid-chest height and get your back well supported. Press forward along the converging path, bring your hands together at the end, and return slowly until your elbows are slightly behind your body.
Press banca agarre neutro mancuernas|With your palms facing each other, your elbows stay close to your body: it loads the triceps more and is easy on the shoulders.|Lie on the bench with the dumbbells over your chest and your palms facing each other. Lower them with your elbows close to your torso until the dumbbells graze the sides of your chest and press up, keeping them parallel.
Press en suelo con barra|Let your elbows touch the floor for an instant without bouncing: the floor marks the end and takes away the stretch.|Lie on the floor under a bar racked low, with your knees bent. Unrack it, lower it until the backs of your arms touch the floor, pause briefly, and press until your arms are straight.
Press en suelo con mancuernas|It's a press without a bench: use the pause on the floor to start without momentum.|Lie on your back with your knees bent and a dumbbell in each hand at chest height. Lower them until your elbows rest on the floor about 45° from your body, stop for an instant, and press up until your arms are straight.
Press banca con pausa|Stop the bar on your chest for a second without relaxing: the pause teaches you to press without a bounce.|With the same setup as the bench press, lower the bar to your chest and hold it still for one or two seconds, keeping your whole body tight. Then press hard until your arms are straight.
Press banca agarre ancho|A wider grip shortens the range and loads the chest more; don't go past twice your shoulder width.|Lie on the bench and grip the bar quite a bit wider than in the regular press, with your forearms vertical at the bottom. Lower the bar to mid-chest with your elbows slightly more flared and press until your arms are straight.
Press banca con bandas|The band adds resistance at the top, where the bar feels easy: accelerate on the way up.|Anchor a band on each side of the bench or rack and loop the ends over the bar. Press as usual: lower under control to your chest and press hard; you'll notice it gets harder the higher you go.
Press de pecho en polea de pie|Step forward with one leg and tighten your abs: your torso shouldn't move as you press.|Set the pulleys at chest height and grab a handle in each hand, facing away from them. With one leg forward, press forward and slightly inward until your hands almost meet, and return slowly with your elbows at shoulder height.
Press de pecho unilateral en polea|Pressing with one arm, your core works to keep you from rotating: hold your torso square.|Facing away from a pulley set at chest height, grab the handle with one hand. Press forward and slightly toward the center until your arm is straight, return slowly, and switch sides when you finish the reps.
Press banca unilateral con mancuerna|Hold on to the bench with your free hand: your body tends to rotate toward the dumbbell side.|Lie down with a dumbbell in one hand and grab the side of the bench with the other. Lower the dumbbell to chest height with your elbow at about 45° and press until your arm is straight, without letting your shoulder lift off the bench.
Press inclinado mancuernas|With the bench at 30°, the upper chest works much more than the shoulder; at a steeper angle the deltoid takes over.|Set the bench at about 30°, sit with the dumbbells on your thighs, and lie back, bringing them to chest height. Press up, bringing them slightly together, and lower slowly until you feel the stretch, with your elbows slightly below the bench.
Press inclinado barra|The bar comes down to the upper chest, below the collarbone, not to the neck.|With the bench at 30-45°, lie back with your shoulder blades squeezed together and grip the bar slightly wider than your shoulders. Unrack it, lower it to your upper chest, and press in a straight line until your arms are straight.
Press inclinado en Smith|Set the bench so the bar lands below your collarbone on the way down: adjust the position until it does.|Put a bench set at about 30° inside the Smith machine. Unlock the bar with a grip slightly wider than your shoulders, lower it under control to your upper chest, and press until your elbows are straight.
Press inclinado en máquina|Press with your whole chest and keep your head against the pad: on a machine, all you have to worry about is the effort.|Adjust the seat so the handles come out at upper-chest height. With your back supported, press forward and up until your arms are almost straight and return slowly until you feel the stretch.
Press inclinado agarre neutro mancuernas|A neutral grip on the incline brings in more triceps and leaves the shoulder in a comfortable position.|With the bench at 30°, hold the dumbbells over your upper chest with your palms facing each other. Lower them with your elbows close to your body to the sides of your chest and press up without letting them touch.
Press inclinado 30° mancuernas|Set the bench at exactly 30°: it's the angle that gives the clavicular part of the chest the most work.|Set the backrest at exactly 30° and lie back with the dumbbells at chest height and your shoulder blades squeezed together. Press up and in until the dumbbells almost meet and lower slowly, with your elbows about 45° from your body.
Press inclinado unilateral mancuerna|Do one arm at a time and hold the bench with your other hand: that's how you fix the weaker side.|With the bench at 30°, hold a dumbbell next to your chest and rest your other hand on the bench. Press up until your arm is straight, lower under control, and finish the set before switching sides.
Press inclinado en polea|Place the incline bench between two low pulleys: the cable pulls from below and keeps tension at the top.|Put a bench set at 30° between two low pulleys and lie back with a handle in each hand at chest height. Press up and toward the center until your hands almost meet and return slowly until you feel the stretch.
Press inclinado con pausa|Pause for two seconds with the bar on your upper chest: you build strength at the hardest point.|On the incline bench, lower the bar to your upper chest and hold it still for two seconds without relaxing your back or shoulders. Press hard out of the pause until your arms are straight.
Aperturas en polea|Imagine you're hugging a tree: your elbows stay fixed and the movement comes from the shoulder.|Set the pulleys at chest height and stand in the middle with a handle in each hand and one leg forward. With your elbows slightly bent, bring your hands together in front of your chest in a wide arc and return slowly until you feel the stretch.
Aperturas mancuernas|Don't lower the dumbbells past chest level: you should feel the stretch in your chest, not in your shoulder.|Lie on a flat bench with the dumbbells over your chest and your palms facing each other. Open them in an arc with your elbows slightly bent until they're at chest height and bring them back up along the same path, as if you were hugging something big.
Cruce de poleas|Cross your hands slightly at the end to squeeze your chest as hard as possible.|With the pulleys set high, grab a handle in each hand and step forward with your torso leaning slightly. Bring your hands down and toward the center in an arc until they cross at waist height and return slowly with your elbows slightly bent.
Pec deck|Get your back well supported and push with the inside of your arms or your elbows, not by pulling with your hands.|Adjust the seat so the handles are at chest height, sit with your back against the pad, and grab the handles or rest your forearms on the pads. Bring your arms together in front until they touch, squeeze for a second, and return slowly until you feel the stretch.
Aperturas inclinadas|With the bench at 30°, the arc works the upper chest: lower until you feel the stretch below your collarbone.|Lie on a bench set at 30° with the dumbbells over your chest and your palms facing each other. Open them in an arc with your elbows slightly bent to chest level and bring them up, squeezing, until they almost touch.
Cruce de poleas bajo|With the pulleys low, bring your hands up toward your chin: you work the upper chest.|Set the pulleys at the lowest position and grab a handle in each hand with one leg forward. Raise your arms in an arc from below, forward and up, until your hands meet at chin height, and lower slowly.
Press Svend|Squeeze the plates between your palms for the whole set: the pressure is what makes the chest work.|Standing, hold one or two plates together between your palms at chest height, squeezing them hard. Extend your arms forward without letting up the squeeze and return slowly to your chest.
Aperturas declinadas mancuernas|On a decline, the arc loads the lower chest: hook your feet securely on the bench.|Lie on a decline bench with your feet secured and the dumbbells over your chest. Open them in an arc with your elbows slightly bent to chest level and bring them up together without letting them clank.
Cruce de poleas a una mano|Working one side at a time, you can cross your hand past the midline and squeeze harder.|Standing sideways to a pulley set at chest height, grab the handle with the near hand. Sweep your arm in an arc forward and across until it passes the middle of your body, return slowly, and switch sides after the set.
Aperturas en banco inclinado con polea|The cables keep tension at the top, where dumbbells weigh almost nothing.|Put an incline bench between two low pulleys and lie back with a handle in each hand. Open your arms in an arc with your elbows slightly bent until you feel the stretch and bring them up, joining your hands over your chest.
Aperturas en suelo con mancuernas|The floor limits the range and protects the shoulder: let your elbows touch down without dropping the weight.|Lie on the floor with your knees bent and the dumbbells over your chest. Open them in an arc until the backs of your arms touch the floor gently and bring them up again, squeezing your chest.
Aperturas con bandas|Anchor the band behind you at chest height and bring your hands together in front without bending your elbows any further.|Loop the band behind your back or tie it to a fixed point behind you at chest height. With your arms open and your elbows slightly bent, bring them together in front in an arc until your hands touch and return slowly.
Fondos|Lean your torso forward and let your elbows flare a little so the chest does the work.|Support yourself on the parallel bars with your arms straight and your body leaning slightly forward. Lower by bending your elbows until your shoulders are slightly below your elbows and press until your arms are straight again.
Flexiones|Keep your body like a plank from head to heels: no sagging hips and no butt in the air.|Place your hands on the floor slightly wider than your shoulders and extend your legs. Lower your chest until it almost touches the floor with your elbows about 45° from your body and press until your arms are straight, without losing your body line.
Flexiones con lastre|Have someone place the plate on your upper back, between your shoulder blades, never on your lower back.|In the push-up position, with a plate or a weighted vest on your upper back, lower your chest until it almost touches the floor and press until your arms are straight, keeping your body straight.
Fondos asistidos en máquina|Use just enough assistance to finish your reps with good technique, and take it away over the weeks.|Choose the counterweight, put your knees or feet on the platform, and hold the handles with your arms straight. Lower by bending your elbows until your shoulders are level with your elbows and press until your arms are straight.
Flexiones con pies elevados|Raising your feet shifts the load to the upper chest and shoulders: the higher, the harder.|Put your feet on a bench or a box and your hands on the floor slightly wider than your shoulders. Lower your chest toward the floor, keeping your body straight, and press until your arms are straight.
Flexiones con manos elevadas|This is the easy version: put your hands on a bench or a wall and lower them as you get stronger.|Place your hands on a bench or a stable surface at the height you need and extend your legs back. Lower your chest toward the edge of the bench with your body straight and press until your arms are straight.
Flexiones en anillas|On the way down, squeeze the rings inward so they don't drift apart: the instability is the challenge.|With the rings close to the floor, support yourself on them with your arms straight and your body in a plank. Lower your chest between the rings, keeping them close to your body, and press until your arms are straight, turning your palms slightly out at the top.
Flexiones arqueras|Shift your weight toward one arm while the other straightens out to the side: it's the step before the one-arm push-up.|Place your hands quite a bit wider than your shoulders. Lower by bringing your chest toward one hand while the opposite arm stays almost straight, press back to the center, and repeat to the other side.
Flexiones con palmada|Push so fast that your hands leave the floor, and land with your elbows slightly bent.|From the push-up position, lower your chest and push explosively to get your hands off the floor. Clap quickly, get your hands back in position, and cushion the landing by bending your elbows before the next rep.
Flexiones en TRX|The more your body leans, the harder it gets: adjust the difficulty by stepping forward or back.|Hold the TRX handles with your arms straight in front of your chest and your body leaning forward. Lower your chest between the handles with your elbows about 45° out and press until your arms are straight, without letting the straps rub your arms.
Dominadas|Start each rep by pulling your shoulders down, away from your ears, before you bend your elbows.|Hang from the bar with your palms facing forward and your hands slightly wider than your shoulders. Pull by driving your elbows down and back until your chin clears the bar and lower slowly until your arms are almost fully straight, without swinging.
Dominadas supinas|With your palms toward you, the biceps work more: come up with your chest toward the bar, not just your chin.|Hang with your palms toward you and your hands shoulder-width apart. Pull with your elbows close to your body until your chest is near the bar and lower under control until your arms are straight.
Dominadas lastradas|Add the weight with a belt, and only once you've mastered 8-10 clean pull-ups.|Attach a plate or a dumbbell to the dip belt and hang from the bar with an overhand grip. Do the full pull-up, chin over the bar, and lower under control so the weight doesn't make you swing.
Dominadas agarre neutro|The grip with your palms facing each other is the easiest on elbows and shoulders: it's usually the one you get the most reps with.|Hang from the parallel handles with your palms facing each other. Pull your chest toward the handles with your elbows close to your body and lower slowly until your arms are straight.
Dominadas asistidas en máquina|Choose the least assistance that lets you finish your reps and reduce it little by little.|Set the counterweight, step onto the platform, and put your knees on the pad with your hands on the handles. Pull until your chin clears the handles and lower slowly, letting the machine only help you, without bouncing at the bottom.
Dominadas con banda|Put the band under one knee or both feet: the thicker the band, the more it helps.|Loop the band over the bar, put a knee or your feet in it, and hang with an overhand grip. Pull until your chin clears the bar and lower under control: the band helps most at the bottom, where it's hardest.
Dominadas agarre ancho|With your hands very wide, the range is short: bring your chest to the bar instead of your chin.|Hang with your hands quite a bit wider than your shoulders and your palms facing forward. Pull by opening your chest and driving your elbows down until your upper chest is close to the bar, and lower slowly.
Dominadas en anillas|Let your palms rotate to neutral as you pull: the rings adapt to your shoulders.|Hang from the rings with your palms facing forward and your arms straight. Pull up, letting the rings rotate until your palms face each other and your chin clears the rings; lower slowly, reversing the rotation.
Dominadas excéntricas|Jump up or use a box and take 3 to 5 seconds to come down: the descent is the whole exercise.|Stand on a box with your chin above the bar and your hands gripping it. Take your feet off and lower as slowly as you can until your arms are straight; get back up using the box.
Dominadas con toalla|Gripping the towel forces you to squeeze hard: it's a back and grip exercise at the same time.|Loop one or two towels over the bar and grab an end in each hand. Pull until your hands are close to your chin and lower slowly without ever easing off your grip.
Remo con barra|Keep your torso at about 45° and bring the bar to your belly button, not your chest, with a neutral back.|Standing with the bar in your hands, bend your knees slightly and hinge at the hips until your torso is at about 45°, with your back straight. Pull the bar toward your belly button, driving your elbows back, and lower it slowly until your arms are straight.
Remo mancuerna|Put a hand and a knee on the bench and pull your elbow toward your hip, like starting a lawnmower.|Put one knee and the hand on the same side on a bench, with your back parallel to the floor. With the other hand, pull the dumbbell by driving your elbow toward your hip, squeeze your back at the top, and lower until your arm is straight.
Remo en polea baja|Sit tall and pull with your elbows: your torso only moves a few degrees.|Sit with your feet on the footrests, your knees slightly bent, and the handle in your hands. Pull toward your abdomen, driving your elbows back and squeezing your shoulder blades together, and return slowly, straightening your arms without rounding your back.
Remo en máquina|Keep your chest against the pad for the whole set: that way your back can't help with momentum.|Adjust the seat so the handles are at chest height and rest your chest on the pad. Pull the handles, driving your elbows back until your shoulder blades come together, and return slowly, straightening your arms.
Remo T|Keep your chest up and your back straight: with your torso bent over, your lower back mustn't round.|Straddle the bar, with the V-handle or the grips under your chest and your torso at about 45°. Pull the bar toward your chest, driving your elbows back, and lower it under control until your arms are straight.
Remo Pendlay|Every rep starts from the floor and goes back to it: pull explosively with your torso parallel to the floor.|With the bar on the floor, bend over until your torso is almost horizontal and grip the bar slightly wider than your shoulders. Pull hard to your lower chest, return the bar to the floor under control, and reset your back before the next rep.
Remo Meadows|Grab the end of the bar with an overhand grip and pull your elbow up and back, flaring it slightly.|With one end of the bar anchored, stand sideways to it with the near foot forward and your torso bent over. Grab the end of the bar with the near hand, pull by driving your elbow up and back, and lower slowly into the stretch.
Remo con apoyo en pecho|With your chest supported on the bench, your lower back is out of the exercise: you can load up without worrying about your back.|Lie face down on an incline bench with a dumbbell hanging from each hand. Pull both by driving your elbows back until they pass your torso, squeeze your shoulder blades together, and lower slowly.
Remo invertido|The more horizontal your body, the harder it is: set the bar height to your level.|Lie under a fixed bar or one in a rack, grip it slightly wider than your shoulders, and straighten your body with your heels on the floor. Pull your chest to the bar with your body straight and lower under control until your arms are straight.
Remo en Smith|The guide rails fix the path: focus on driving your elbows back and squeezing your shoulder blades together.|Set the Smith bar at knee height, grip it slightly wider than your shoulders, and bend your torso to about 45° with your back straight. Pull toward your belly button, squeeze your back, and lower the bar slowly.
Remo con barra agarre supino|With your palms up, your elbows stay close to your body and the lower lats work more.|With your torso at about 45° and your knees slightly bent, grip the bar with your palms up at shoulder width. Pull toward your lower abdomen with your elbows close to your body and lower slowly.
Remo en polea agarre neutro|The V-handle puts your palms facing each other: pull toward your belly button with your elbows brushing your sides.|Seated at the low pulley with the V-handle, back straight and knees slightly bent, pull the handle toward your belly button with your elbows close to your body. Squeeze your shoulder blades together for a second and return slowly, straightening your arms.
Remo unilateral en polea|Working one arm, you can reach farther forward and bring your elbow farther back: use the whole range.|Standing or seated facing a pulley at mid height, grab the handle with one hand. Pull by driving your elbow back and close to your body, rotate your torso a little only at the end, and return by reaching your arm forward.
Remo unilateral en máquina|Brace yourself with your free hand and don't rotate your torso: all the movement comes from the shoulder and elbow.|Set the machine with your chest supported and grab one handle with one hand. Pull the handle by driving your elbow back, squeeze your back at the top, and return slowly. Finish one side before switching.
Remo en anillas|Turn your palms in as you pull and keep your body rigid, like in a plank.|Hold the rings with your arms straight and your body leaning back, straight from head to heels. Pull your chest toward the rings with your elbows back, and lower slowly until your arms are straight.
Remo Kroc|It's a heavy, high-rep one-arm row: some momentum is allowed, but your back is in charge.|Rest one hand on a bench or a support, with your torso leaning slightly and your feet apart. Pull a heavy dumbbell hard toward your hip, allowing a slight torso rotation, and lower it to a full stretch.
Remo con banda|Anchor the band at chest height and squeeze your shoulder blades together at the end, holding for a second.|Fix the band to a point at chest height and hold one end in each hand. Step back until you feel tension and pull by driving your elbows back, close to your body; return slowly until your arms are straight.
Remo en polea alta|Pull toward your upper chest with your elbows flared: you work the upper back and the rhomboids.|Set the pulley slightly above head height with a bar or a rope and sit or stand in front of it. Pull toward your upper chest with your elbows flared away from your body, squeeze your shoulder blades together, and return slowly.
Remo en máquina convergente|The handles come together at the end: use that to squeeze your back, bringing your elbows behind your body.|Sit with your chest against the pad and grab the handles. Pull along the converging path until your elbows are behind your torso, hold for a second, and return slowly until your arms are straight.
Remo alto en máquina|Pull down and back toward the sides of your chest with your elbows close to your body: it's a row from above that targets the lats.|Sit with your chest against the pad and grab the handles, which sit high and in front of you, with your arms straight. Pull by driving your elbows down and back until your hands reach the sides of your chest, squeeze your shoulder blades for a second, and return slowly until your arms are straight.
Jalón al pecho|Pull your elbows toward your pockets and lean back a little, without swinging.|Sit with your thighs under the pads and grip the bar slightly wider than your shoulders. Pull toward your upper chest, driving your elbows down and back, squeeze your back, and let the bar rise slowly until your arms are straight.
Jalón agarre estrecho|With your hands close together, the range is long: stretch all the way at the top before each pull.|Attach a close-grip handle, sit with your thighs secured, and straighten your arms. Pull toward your upper chest with your elbows close to your body, leaning back only slightly, and rise slowly to a full stretch.
Jalón unilateral|Pull with one arm at a time, driving your elbow toward your hip: that way you feel each lat better.|Attach a single handle to the high pulley and sit with your thighs secured. Pull with one hand, driving your elbow down and toward your hip, rotate your torso a little at the end, and rise slowly until your arm is straight.
Jalón agarre neutro|The grip with your palms facing each other lets you go heavier: pull with your elbow, not your hand.|With the neutral-grip handle, sit down and straighten your arms. Pull toward your upper chest, driving your elbows toward your ribs, and return slowly to the top until you feel the stretch in your lats.
Jalón agarre supino|With your palms toward you, your elbows come down close to your body: be careful not to turn it into a curl.|Grip the bar with your palms toward you at shoulder width and sit with your thighs secured. Pull toward your upper chest with your elbows close to your torso and rise under control until your arms are straight.
Jalón agarre ancho|Open your hands wide and bring the bar to your collarbone: the short range calls for control, not momentum.|Grip the bar quite a bit wider than your shoulders and sit with your thighs secured. Pull to your upper chest, opening your chest and driving your elbows down to the sides, and rise slowly.
Jalón en máquina convergente|The handles come down toward the center along a natural arc: pull until your elbows reach your sides.|Adjust the seat and the pads, and grab the handles with your arms straight overhead. Pull along the machine's path until your hands reach shoulder height and rise slowly.
Jalón en máquina unilateral|Work one side at a time and push your chest toward the handle at the end of the pull.|Sit in the machine with your thighs secured and grab one handle with one hand. Pull by driving your elbow down and back to shoulder height, hold for an instant, and rise slowly. Switch sides when you finish.
Jalón con cuerda|Spread the ends of the rope on the way down to bring your elbows farther back than with a bar.|Attach a rope to the high pulley and sit or kneel in front of it with your arms straight. Pull toward your upper chest, spreading the ends of the rope and driving your elbows toward your sides, and rise slowly.
Jalón arrodillado a una mano|On your knees you can't help with your legs: pull your elbow toward your hip with your torso still.|Kneel in front of the high pulley with a single handle in one hand. Pull by driving your elbow down and toward the hip on the same side, squeeze your lat, and rise slowly until your arm is straight.
Peso muerto|Push the floor away with your legs and keep the bar against your body the whole way.|Stand with the bar over your midfoot, squat down, and grip it at shoulder width with your back straight and your chest up. Push the floor away with your legs and extend your hips, keeping the bar against your legs until you're standing tall; lower it along the same path.
Hiperextensiones|Come up until your body is in line, no further: over-arching your back at the top adds no work and loads the lower back.|Set up on the back extension bench with your hips at the edge of the pad and your feet secured. Lower your torso by bending at the hips with your back straight and come up by contracting your glutes and lower back until your body forms a line.
Peso muerto con barra hexagonal|You stand inside the bar: the weight sits at your center and your back works less than in the conventional deadlift.|Step inside the trap bar and grab the handles with your palms facing each other. With your back straight and your hips a bit lower than in the deadlift, push the floor away with your legs until you're standing tall, and lower slowly.
Peso muerto con déficit|Standing on a plate, the range is longer: use less load than in your regular deadlift.|Stand on a plate or a 3-5 cm platform with the bar over your midfoot. Squat down lower than in the regular deadlift with your back straight, grip the bar, and lift it by pushing the floor away until you're standing tall.
Rack pull|Set the bar at knee height and lock out at the top by squeezing your glutes.|Set the bar on the rack supports just above or below your knees. Grip it with your back straight, drive your hips forward until you're standing tall, and return it to the supports under control.
Peso muerto con pausa|Stop the bar for a couple of seconds just below your knees: it forces you to keep your back locked in.|Start the deadlift and hold the bar at knee height for two seconds, with your back straight and the bar close. Finish the lift until you're standing tall and lower without rushing.
Hiperextensiones a 45°|Round your upper back a little and think about pushing your hips into the pad: that way the glutes work more.|Set up on the 45° bench with your hips slightly above the pad and your feet secured. Lower your torso by bending at the hips and come up by squeezing your glutes until your body is in line with your legs.
Hiperextensiones con lastre|Hold the plate against your chest with your arms crossed: the load should stay close to your body.|On the back extension bench, hug a plate against your chest. Lower your torso with your back straight by bending at the hips and come up with your glutes and lower back until your body lines up with your legs.
Hiperextensiones inversas|Here the legs move, not the torso: raise them with your glutes to horizontal.|Lie face down on a high bench or the reverse hyper machine, with your hips at the edge and your hands holding on. Raise your straight legs until they're in line with your torso, squeezing your glutes, and lower them slowly.
Extensión lumbar en máquina|Move your back slowly and under control, with no jerking: it's an endurance exercise, not a max-strength one.|Sit in the machine with your upper back against the pad and your feet secured. Push back by extending your spine until you're almost straight and return slowly forward.
Superman|Raise your arms and legs together just a few centimeters and hold: there's no need to arch a lot.|Lie face down with your arms extended in front of you. Raise your arms, chest, and legs a few centimeters off the floor at the same time, squeezing your glutes and back, hold for two seconds, and lower slowly.
Sentadilla|Break at the hips and knees together and push your knees out, in line with your toes.|With the bar on your upper back and your feet shoulder-width apart, take a breath and brace your abs. Lower by bending your hips and knees together, chest up, until your thighs are at least parallel to the floor, and come up by pushing the floor away with your whole foot.
Sentadilla frontal|Keep your elbows high the whole time: if they drop, the bar rolls forward and your back rounds.|Rest the bar on the front of your shoulders, close to your neck, with your elbows high and your fingers under the bar. Lower with your torso very upright to the bottom and come up by driving with your quads without letting your chest drop.
Sentadilla en Smith|Put your feet a little in front of the bar: that way you go straight down without your knees traveling far forward.|Set the Smith bar on your upper back with your feet slightly in front of your body. Unlock the bar, lower by bending your hips and knees until your thighs are parallel, and come up by pushing with your whole foot.
Sentadilla con pausa|Pause for two seconds at the bottom without relaxing: the pause takes away the bounce and makes you come up on strength alone.|Do the regular squat and, when you reach the bottom, stay still for two seconds with your abs braced and your back straight. From the pause, drive up hard, pushing the floor away until your legs are straight.
Sentadilla en caja|Sit on the box without dropping onto it and start without rocking: the box marks the same depth every time.|Place a box or a bench behind you at the height you want to squat to. With the bar on your back, lower by sitting your hips back until you sit gently on the box, keep tension for an instant, and come up by driving with your legs.
Sentadilla Zercher|Hold the bar in the crook of your elbows and hug your torso: your core works a ton.|Set the bar in the rack at abdomen height and hold it in the crook of your elbows, with your hands together. Lower with your torso upright until your thighs are parallel and come up keeping the bar close to your body.
Sentadilla con barra de seguridad|The bar with front handles lets your shoulders relax: don't pull it down, just guide it.|Set the safety bar on your back with the pads on your shoulders and hold the handles in front. Lower, keeping your chest up, to full depth and come up by pushing the floor away; the bar tends to tip you forward, so resist with your upper back.
Sentadilla con mancuernas|Let the dumbbells hang at your sides and lower with your back straight: the lower you go, the more the glutes work.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand at your sides and your feet shoulder-width apart, lower by bending your hips and knees until your thighs are parallel. Come up by pushing through your heels and midfoot.
Sentadilla goblet con mancuerna|Hold the dumbbell against your chest and use your elbows to push your knees out at the bottom.|Hold a dumbbell vertically against your chest with both hands. Lower between your legs with your torso upright until your elbows brush the inside of your knees and come up by pushing with your whole foot.
Sentadilla sumo con mancuerna|Set your feet wide with your toes pointed out: the adductors and glutes work more.|With your feet quite a bit wider than your shoulders and your toes pointed out, hold a dumbbell with both hands hanging between your legs. Lower straight down, with your knees tracking over your toes, and come up squeezing your glutes.
Sentadilla con bandas|The band is heavier at the top: use it to finish each rep strong.|Step on the band with your feet shoulder-width apart and loop it behind your neck or over your shoulders. Lower until your thighs are parallel and come up by pushing the floor away against the resistance, which increases as you stand.
Prensa|Don't let your lower back come off the pad on the way down: stop just before your hips lift.|Sit with your back well supported and your feet in the middle of the platform at shoulder width. Release the safeties, lower the platform by bending your knees to about 90° or a bit more, and push with your whole foot without locking your knees at the top.
Hack squat|Get your back well supported and go all the way down: the machine lets you work the quads with your back protected.|Set up with your back and shoulders against the pads and your feet in the middle of the platform. Release the safeties, lower by bending your knees until your thighs are parallel or lower, and come up by pushing with your whole foot.
Prensa unilateral|With one leg at a time you find out if one side is weaker: always start with your weaker leg.|Sit in the leg press and put just one foot in the middle of the platform, with the other leg off it. Lower to about 90° at the knee with your foot flat and push through your heel and midfoot; repeat with the other leg.
Prensa horizontal|Push with your whole foot and don't let your knees cave in as you straighten.|Sit in the horizontal leg press with your back supported and your feet on the platform hip-width apart. Push until your legs are almost straight and return slowly, bending your knees to about 90°.
Prensa con pies bajos|With your feet low on the platform, the knee travels farther forward and the quads take almost all the work.|Place your feet on the lower part of the platform, hip-width apart. Lower under control until you feel the stretch without your heels lifting, and push until your legs are almost straight.
Prensa con pies juntos|With your feet together, the outer thigh works more: go less deep if you feel your hips lifting.|Put your feet together in the middle of the platform, toes pointing forward. Lower the platform by bending your knees to about 90° and push hard, keeping your knees in line with your feet.
Hack squat inverso|Facing the machine, the movement loads the glutes and hamstrings more: push your hips back on the way down.|Stand facing the hack squat's back pad, with your chest against the pad and your shoulders under the supports. Lower by sitting your hips back and down until your thighs are parallel and come up by extending your hips and knees.
Hack squat en Smith|Put your feet forward and lean your back into the Smith bar to mimic the hack squat: the knee leads.|Set up in the Smith machine with the bar on your upper back and your feet well in front of your body, together or hip-width apart. Lower with your torso straight until your thighs are parallel and come up by pushing with your whole foot.
Sentadilla Pendulum|The pendulum machine lets you go very deep with little load on your back: use the full range.|Set up in the machine with your back against the pad and your shoulders under the supports. Lower, letting the platform follow its arc to the bottom, with your heels down, and come up by pushing without locking your knees.
Sentadilla en máquina|Follow the machine's path without your back coming off the pad: it's a guided squat so you can focus on your legs.|Adjust the supports to your height and set up with your back against the pad and your feet on the platform. Lower until your thighs are parallel and come up by pushing with your whole foot until your legs are almost straight.
Zancadas|Take a long step and drop straight down: the back knee almost grazes the floor and your torso stays upright.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand, take a long step forward. Lower your back knee toward the floor until both knees are at about 90° and push off the front foot to return to the start; alternate legs.
Sentadilla búlgara|Rest the top of your back foot on the bench and let the weight fall on the front leg.|Facing away from a bench, rest the top of your back foot on it and step the other leg forward. With a dumbbell in each hand, drop straight down until your front thigh is parallel and come up by pushing through the front heel.
Step up|Step up with the leg that's on the box, without pushing off the bottom leg.|Place your whole foot on a box or a bench at knee height. With a dumbbell in each hand, step up by pushing with the top foot until the leg is straight and lower the other leg slowly to the floor.
Zancada caminando|Move forward step by step without bringing your feet together between lunges: torso upright and eyes ahead.|With a dumbbell in each hand, take a long step forward and lower your back knee until it almost touches the floor. Push with the front leg to move straight into the next lunge with the other leg.
Pistol asistida|Hold on to a post or a TRX only as much as you need to lower under control on one leg.|Standing on one leg, with the other extended in front, hold on to a support or straps. Lower by bending the standing knee as far as you can with your heel on the floor and come up using your arms as little as possible.
Zancada en Smith|The guided bar gives you balance: focus on dropping straight down and pushing with the front leg.|Set the Smith bar on your back and step one leg forward with a long step. Lower your back knee toward the floor until the front one is at 90° and come up by pushing with the front foot; finish one side and switch.
Zancada con barra|With the bar on your back, balance is harder: step hip-width apart, not in a line.|With the bar on your upper back, take a long step forward with your feet hip-width apart. Lower your back knee until it almost touches the floor and come back by pushing with the front leg.
Step up lateral|Step up onto the box sideways: it works the gluteus medius and knee stability.|Stand sideways next to a low box and put your near foot on it. Step up by pushing with that leg until it's straight and lower the other leg slowly to the floor, without letting the top knee cave in.
Sentadilla búlgara en Smith|The guide rails let you load more without thinking about balance: put the bench one long step from the bar.|With the Smith bar on your back, rest the top of your back foot on a bench and step the other leg forward. Drop straight down until your front thigh is parallel and come up by pushing through your heel.
Zancada con salto|Switch legs in the air and land softly, with your front knee over your foot.|From the lunge position, jump up hard, switch your legs in the air, and land in a lunge with the other leg in front, cushioning the landing. Link the jumps without pausing.
Sentadilla búlgara con barra|Get the bar on your back before you put your foot on the bench, and lower with your torso upright.|With the bar on your upper back, rest the top of your back foot on a bench and step the other leg forward. Drop straight down until your front thigh is parallel and come up by pushing with the front leg.
Zancada frontal con déficit|Putting your front foot on a plate lengthens the range: lower until your back knee goes below foot level.|Place your front foot on a plate or a low step and take a long step. With a dumbbell in each hand, lower your back knee below the level of the step and come up by pushing with the front leg.
Extensión cuádriceps|Hold for a second at the top with your legs straight and lower over two or three seconds.|Sit with your back supported, your knees at the edge of the seat, and the pad on your ankles. Straighten your legs fully, squeeze your quads for an instant, and lower slowly without dropping the weight.
Sissy squat|Lean back while your knees travel forward: the quads work in a stretch with no weight.|Standing, hold on to a support with one hand and rise onto your toes. Lean your torso back while your knees move forward and down, with your hips extended, as far as you can control, and come back up.
Extensión una pierna|One leg at a time evens out the strength of both quads: start with the weaker one.|Adjust the leg extension machine and place the pad on just one ankle. Straighten your leg fully, squeeze for a second, and lower slowly; do all your reps and switch legs.
Extensión con pausa|Hold for three seconds with your legs straight: the pause at the top is what makes the quads burn.|On the leg extension machine, straighten your legs and hold the contraction for three seconds with your knees locked. Lower slowly and go up again without resting at the bottom.
Extensión con banda|Anchor the band behind you at ankle height and straighten your knee all the way against the resistance.|Sitting on a bench or a chair, tie the band to a leg of the seat and to your ankle. Extend your leg forward until it's straight, hold for a second, and slowly bend your knee again.
Extensión de rodilla en polea|With the ankle strap on the low pulley, the cable gives tension through the knee's whole range.|Attach an ankle strap to the low pulley and sit on a bench facing away from it. Straighten your knee until your leg is straight, squeeze your quads, and return slowly to 90°.
Peso muerto rumano|Push your hips back as if you were closing a door with your butt; your knees barely bend.|Standing with the bar in your hands and your knees slightly bent, lower the bar along your thighs by pushing your hips back with your back straight. Stop when you feel the stretch in your hamstrings, around mid-shin, and come up by driving your hips forward.
Buenos días|Start light: the load is on your back and the lever arm is long.|With the bar on your upper back and your knees slightly bent, lean your torso forward by pushing your hips back with your back straight, almost to horizontal. Come back up squeezing your glutes and hamstrings.
Peso muerto sumo|Set your feet very wide and push the floor apart: your torso stays more upright than in the conventional deadlift.|Stand with your feet very wide and your toes pointed out, and grip the bar with your hands between your legs. With your chest up and your knees out over your feet, push the floor away until you're standing tall and lower the bar along the same path.
Peso muerto rumano mancuernas|The dumbbells travel down in front of your legs, brushing your thighs: don't let them drift away from your body.|With a dumbbell in each hand in front of your thighs and your knees slightly bent, lower by pushing your hips back with your back straight until you feel the stretch in your hamstrings. Come up by driving your hips forward and squeezing your glutes.
Good morning sentado|Seated, your legs don't take part: the movement is all hips and back, so go slowly.|Straddle a bench with the bar on your upper back and your feet planted. Lean your torso forward with your back straight as far as your flexibility allows and come back up by contracting your glutes and lower back.
Peso muerto rumano a una pierna|The free leg rises behind you as you lower: your body moves like a seesaw.|Standing on one leg with a dumbbell in the opposite hand, lean your torso forward while the other leg rises straight behind you. Lower until your torso is almost horizontal, with your hips level, and come back up squeezing the glute of the standing leg.
Peso muerto rumano en Smith|In the Smith machine the bar travels straight down: stand a little away from the bar so you can push your hips back.|Hold the Smith bar at thigh height with your knees slightly bent. Unlock it and lower it by pushing your hips back with your back straight until you feel the stretch; come up by driving your hips forward.
Peso muerto con piernas rígidas|Your knees barely bend: go only as low as you can keep your back straight.|With the bar in your hands and your legs almost straight, lean your torso forward from the hips, letting the bar travel down close to your legs. Stop when your back starts to round and come up with your hamstrings and glutes.
Peso muerto rumano con kettlebell|Hold the kettlebell by the handle with both hands between your legs and lower by pushing your hips back.|Standing with your feet hip-width apart and the kettlebell hanging in front of you, bend your knees slightly and lower by pushing your hips back with your back straight. Come up squeezing your glutes until you're standing tall.
Pull-through en polea|Facing away from the pulley, the cable pulls your hips back: finish each rep by squeezing your glutes.|Attach a rope to the low pulley, face away from it, and hold the rope between your legs. Take a few steps forward, lower by pushing your hips back with your back straight, and stand tall again by driving your hips forward.
Peso muerto rumano con banda|Step on the band with both feet: the resistance grows on the way up, right where the glutes squeeze hardest.|Step on the middle of the band with your feet hip-width apart and hold the ends. Lower by pushing your hips back with your back straight and your knees slightly bent into the stretch, and come up squeezing your glutes.
Curl femoral|Keep your hips tight against the bench or seat: if they lift, the hamstrings work less.|Adjust the machine so your knee lines up with the pivot and the pad sits just above your heel. Bend your knees, bringing the pad toward your glutes, squeeze for a second, and return slowly until your legs are almost straight.
Curl femoral sentado|Seated, the hamstrings start more stretched: it's the version that grows them most, so go all the way down.|Sit with your back supported, the pad on your ankles, and the thigh pad snug. Bend your knees, pushing the pad down and back, and return slowly until your legs are almost fully straight.
Curl nórdico|Lower as slowly as you can with your hips extended; when you can't hold it anymore, catch yourself with your hands.|Kneel with your ankles held by a partner or a support and keep your body straight from knees to head. Let yourself fall forward as slowly as possible, braking with your hamstrings, catch yourself with your hands, and push off to come back.
Curl femoral a una pierna|One leg at a time: let the other one hang relaxed and don't use it to help.|On the leg curl machine, place the pad on just one ankle. Bend that knee to the end of the range, squeeze, and lower slowly; repeat with the other leg.
Curl femoral de pie|Standing, the hips tend to drift back: keep your thigh against the pad the whole way.|Set up in the standing machine with your thigh supported and the pad behind your ankle. Bend your knee, bringing your heel toward your glute, and lower slowly. Finish one leg before switching.
Curl femoral con balón suizo|Keep your hips up while you roll the ball in: if they drop, the hamstrings are out of the exercise.|Lie on your back with your heels on a Swiss ball and raise your hips until your body is in line. Without lowering your hips, bend your knees to roll the ball toward your glutes and straighten your legs again slowly.
Curl femoral deslizante|With your heels on towels or sliders, the key is straightening your legs slowly.|Lie on your back with your heels on sliders and raise your hips. Drag your heels toward your glutes by bending your knees and slowly extend them again without letting your hips touch the floor.
Curl femoral con mancuerna|Hold the dumbbell firmly between your feet and come up slowly: if it shifts, use less weight.|Lie face down on a bench with a dumbbell held between your feet. Bend your knees, bringing the dumbbell toward your glutes under control, and lower it slowly until your legs are almost straight.
Curl femoral con banda|Tie the band to something low and fixed and move away until it's taut from the start.|Lie face down with the band tied to a fixed point and to your ankle. Bend your knee, bringing your heel toward your glute against the resistance, and slowly straighten your leg again.
Hip thrust|Tuck your chin and look forward as you come up: that sets your pelvis right and you squeeze the glutes harder.|Rest your upper back on a bench, with the bar over your hips, padded, and your feet hip-width apart. Push through your heels, raising your hips until your torso and thighs are in line, squeeze your glutes for a second, and lower.
Patada de glúteo en polea|Move your leg back without arching your back: the movement ends when the glute squeezes.|Attach an ankle strap to the low pulley and hold on to the frame with your torso leaning slightly. Move your leg back with the knee almost straight until your thigh passes the line of your body, squeeze your glute, and return slowly.
Puente de glúteo|Push through your heels and raise your hips without arching your lower back.|Lie on your back with your knees bent and your feet flat, close to your glutes. Push through your heels, raising your hips until your knees, hips, and shoulders are in line, squeeze your glutes for two seconds, and lower slowly.
Hip thrust unilateral|With one leg in the air, your hips tend to rotate: keep them level as if you were balancing a glass on them.|Rest your upper back on a bench and plant one foot on the floor with the other leg bent in the air. Push through the planted heel, raising your hips to horizontal, squeeze your glute, and lower slowly.
Extensión de cadera máquina|Push back and down with your heel, without rotating your hips or arching your back.|Set up in the machine with the pad behind your working leg and hold the handles. Push your leg back by extending your hip until your thigh is in line with your body and return slowly.
Hip thrust en máquina|The machine saves you from setting up the bar: focus on the pause at the top with your glutes squeezed.|Sit in the machine with your back against the pad and the belt or pad over your hips. Push through your heels until your hips are fully extended, squeeze for a second, and lower slowly.
Hip thrust en Smith|The guide rails stabilize the bar: set the bench so the bar lands right over your hips.|Put a bench inside the Smith machine and rest your upper back on it with the bar over your hips, padded. Push through your heels, raising your hips until your torso and thighs are in line, and lower under control.
Hip thrust con banda|Run the band over your hips and fix the ends under your feet or to anchors: squeeze at the top.|Rest your upper back on a bench with the band over your hips, anchored to the floor on both sides. Push through your heels until your hips are fully extended against the band, hold for a second, and lower.
Puente de glúteo a una pierna|Extend one leg toward the ceiling or straight ahead and raise your hips with the other glute only.|Lie on your back with one knee bent and that foot flat, and the other leg straight. Push through the planted heel, raising your hips without letting them tilt to one side, squeeze your glute, and lower slowly.
Hip thrust con mancuerna|Hold the dumbbell on your hips with both hands so it doesn't roll as you come up.|Rest your upper back on a bench and place a dumbbell horizontally over your hips, holding it with your hands. Push through your heels until your torso and thighs are in line, squeeze your glutes, and lower.
Patada de glúteo en máquina|Keep your torso against the pad and push the platform with your heel, not your toes.|Set up in the kickback machine with your forearms or chest supported and one foot on the platform. Push back and up by extending your hip until your thigh is in line with your body and return slowly.
Patada de glúteo a cuatro apoyos|Raise your leg with the knee at 90° as if you wanted to leave a footprint on the ceiling.|Get on all fours with your hands under your shoulders and your knees under your hips. Raise one leg with the knee bent until your thigh is parallel to the floor, without arching your back, and lower it slowly.
Donkey kick con banda|Loop the band around the sole of your foot and your hands: the resistance increases at the end, where the glute squeezes.|On all fours, hold the band under your hands and loop it around the sole of one foot. Push that foot back and up by extending your hip against the band and return slowly with your knee under your hip.
Hip thrust con pausa|Hold for three seconds at the top with your hips extended: if the bar sinks during the pause, it's too heavy.|Set up as for the hip thrust, raise your hips until your torso and thighs are in line, and hold the position for three seconds, squeezing your glutes. Lower slowly and repeat.
Puente de glúteo con banda|The band above your knees makes you push them out: you work the gluteus medius too.|Lie on your back with a mini band above your knees and your feet flat. Push your knees slightly apart against the band and, without letting them close, raise your hips by pushing through your heels; squeeze at the top and lower.
Gemelo de pie|Lower your heels to a full stretch and come up without bouncing: the pause at the bottom is what builds the most.|Set up in the machine with your shoulders under the pads and the balls of your feet on the edge of the platform. Lower your heels as far as you can, pause for a second, and rise onto your toes as high as possible, squeezing your calves.
Gemelo en prensa|Put only the balls of your feet on the platform and don't bend your knees as you push.|Sit in the leg press with your legs almost straight and place the balls of your feet on the lower edge of the platform. Push by extending your ankles and return slowly until you feel the stretch in your calves.
Gemelo a una pierna|Rest a hand on the wall for balance and rise as high as you can on one foot.|Standing on one foot on the edge of a step, hold on to something with your hand. Lower your heel below the step and rise onto your toes as high as possible; finish the set before switching feet.
Gemelo burro|With your torso bent over, the calves work in a deep stretch: lower your heels all the way on every rep.|Set up in the donkey calf machine with your hips under the pad and your torso leaning forward, with the balls of your feet on the platform. Lower your heels into the stretch and rise onto your toes.
Gemelo en Smith|Put a plate or a step under your feet inside the Smith machine so you can lower your heels.|Set the Smith bar on your back and the balls of your feet on a step. Unlock the bar, lower your heels into the stretch, and rise onto your toes as high as you can.
Gemelo con mancuerna a una pierna|Hold the dumbbell on the side of the working leg and support yourself with the other hand.|Standing on a step on one foot with a dumbbell in the hand on the same side, lower your heel below the step and rise onto your toes to the top. Switch sides when the set is done.
Gemelo con barra|With the bar on your back, go up and down slowly: balance is part of the exercise.|With the bar on your upper back, put the balls of your feet on a plate or a low step. Lower your heels under control and rise onto your toes as high as possible, keeping your body straight.
Gemelo en escalón|With no weight, do lots of reps through the full range with a pause at each end.|Standing with the balls of your feet on the edge of a step and one hand on the wall, lower your heels below the step and rise onto your toes as high as possible, holding for a second at the top.
Saltos de gemelo|Jump with your ankles only, knees almost straight, and bounce quickly off the floor.|Standing with your feet hip-width apart, do short, continuous jumps using mostly your ankles, with your knees almost straight. Land on the balls of your feet and take off again right away.
Gemelo de pie unilateral en máquina|The machine lets you load one leg safely: lower your heel slowly all the way down.|Set up in the standing calf machine and put just one foot on the platform, with the other leg bent. Lower your heel into the stretch and rise onto your toes; repeat on the other side.
Gemelo sentado|With the knee bent, the soleus does the work: do slow reps through the full range.|Sit in the machine with your knees under the pad and the balls of your feet on the platform. Lower your heels as far as you can and raise them as high as possible, with a pause at each end.
Gemelo sentado unilateral|One leg at a time lets you lower the heel farther: compare the height each side reaches.|On the seated calf machine, place just one foot on the platform with the knee under the pad. Lower your heel into the stretch and rise onto your toes; switch legs when you finish.
Gemelo sentado con barra|Put a pad or a towel between the bar and your knees and place your feet on a plate.|Seated on a bench, put the balls of your feet on a plate and the bar across your knees, padded. Lower your heels to the floor and raise them onto your toes, pushing the bar up.
Gemelo sentado con mancuerna|Stand the dumbbell on your knee and hold it with your hand so it doesn't move.|Sit on a bench with the ball of one foot on a plate and a dumbbell resting on that knee. Lower your heel into the stretch and raise it onto your toes; switch legs after the set.
Curl bíceps barra|Keep your elbows pinned to your sides: if they drift forward, the shoulders start helping.|Standing with the straight bar in your hands, palms up at shoulder width, bend your elbows to bring the bar up to your chest without swinging your torso. Squeeze your biceps at the top and lower slowly until your arms are straight.
Curl con barra Z|The EZ bar leaves your wrists slightly turned and more comfortable: use it if the straight bar bothers you.|Hold the EZ bar on the inner curves with your palms up. With your elbows at your sides, bring the bar up to chest height, squeeze for an instant, and lower it under control over two or three seconds.
Curl con barra agarre ancho|With your hands wider than your shoulders, the short (inner) head of the biceps works more.|Grip the bar with your palms up and your hands slightly wider than your shoulders. Raise the bar by bending your elbows without moving them, squeeze at the top, and lower slowly.
Curl con barra agarre estrecho|Hands close together load the long (outer) head more: don't let your elbows flare.|Grip the bar with your palms up and your hands about 15-20 cm apart. Bend your elbows to bring the bar up to your chest, with your elbows still at your sides, and lower under control.
Curl con barra Z agarre cerrado|Use the EZ bar's outer curves for a close grip without straining your wrists.|Hold the EZ bar on the curves closest to the center. With your elbows tucked in to your torso, bring the bar up to your chest and lower it slowly until your arms are almost straight.
Curl 21|It's 7 reps of the bottom half, 7 of the top half, and 7 full ones, with no rest in between.|With an EZ bar or a straight bar, do 7 reps from straight arms up to 90°, 7 from 90° up to your chest, and 7 through the full range. Use less weight than usual and don't rest between the parts.
Curl en Smith|The guided bar only goes up and down: use that to focus on squeezing your biceps with no swinging.|Stand facing the Smith machine with the bar at thigh height and grip it with your palms up. Unlock it and curl by bending your elbows up to your chest; lower slowly and lock it again when you finish.
Curl martillo|With your palms facing each other, the brachialis and forearm do the work: raise the dumbbell like a hammer.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand and your palms facing each other, bend your elbows to bring the dumbbells toward your shoulders without rotating your wrists. Lower slowly with your elbows close to your body.
Curl martillo en cuerda|The rope on the low pulley gives constant tension: spread the ends slightly at the top.|Attach a rope to the low pulley and hold it with your palms facing each other. Curl by bending your elbows until your hands reach shoulder height, spreading the ends slightly, and lower slowly.
Curl martillo cruzado|Bring the dumbbell diagonally toward the opposite side of your chest: the brachialis works from a different angle.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand and a neutral grip, raise one dumbbell across the front of your body toward the opposite shoulder. Lower it slowly and repeat with the other arm.
Curl martillo alterno|Raise one arm at a time and don't let your torso turn toward the working side.|Standing with a neutral grip, raise one dumbbell by bending your elbow up to your shoulder while the other stays down. Lower under control and alternate arms on each rep.
Curl martillo en banco inclinado|Seated on an incline, the arm starts behind your body and the brachialis works in a deep stretch.|Sit on a bench set at about 45° with your arms hanging and the dumbbells with your palms facing each other. Raise the dumbbells without letting your elbows move forward and lower them slowly until your arms are fully straight.
Curl martillo con barra Z|Hold the EZ bar by its neutral grips if it has them, or by the curves, with your thumbs up.|Hold the bar with a neutral or semi-neutral grip and your elbows at your sides. Bend your elbows to bring the bar up to your chest and lower it under control without swinging your torso.
Curl predicador|Get the backs of your arms well supported on the pad and don't lift your elbows as you curl.|Sit at the preacher bench with your armpits over the edge of the pad and grip the EZ bar with your palms up. Raise the bar by bending your elbows and lower it slowly until your arms are almost straight, without fully locking out.
Curl spider|Lie face down on an incline bench with your arms hanging: that way the biceps can't cheat.|Lie face down on an incline bench with your arms hanging straight down and a dumbbell in each hand. Raise the dumbbells by bending your elbows without moving them forward, squeeze at the top, and lower slowly.
Curl predicador con mancuerna|One arm at a time on the pad lets you focus on each arm: turn your wrist slightly outward at the top.|Rest one arm on the pad with a dumbbell and your palm up. Raise the dumbbell by bending your elbow, squeeze your biceps at the top, and lower it slowly until your arm is almost straight; repeat with the other arm.
Curl predicador en polea|Put the preacher bench in front of a low pulley: the cable pulls even with your arm bent.|Place the preacher bench facing a low pulley with a short bar. Rest your arms on the pad, raise the bar by bending your elbows, and lower it slowly until your arms are almost straight.
Curl Scott con barra recta|With the straight bar, the wrist rotates more: if it bothers you, switch to the EZ bar.|Sit at the Scott bench with your arms on the pad and grip the straight bar with your palms up. Raise the bar by bending your elbows and lower it under control until your arms are almost straight.
Press francés|Lower the bar toward your forehead moving only your elbows, and keep them pointing at the ceiling.|Lie on a flat bench with the EZ bar over your chest and your arms straight. Bend your elbows to bring the bar toward your forehead or just behind your head, without letting them flare out, and straighten your arms to come back up.
Extensión sobre la cabeza|Hold the dumbbell with both hands by one end and let it travel down behind your head into the stretch.|Seated or standing, hold a dumbbell with both hands overhead with your arms straight. Lower the dumbbell behind your head by bending your elbows, which point up, and straighten your arms to come up.
Rompecráneos barra Z|Bring the bar slightly behind your head rather than to your forehead: the triceps work in a deeper stretch.|Lie on a flat bench holding the EZ bar with a close grip and your arms straight over your chest. Tilt your arms back slightly and lower the bar toward the top of your head by bending your elbows; straighten your arms to come up.
Extensión sobre la cabeza con cuerda|Facing away from the pulley, lean forward and extend your arms overhead, spreading the rope.|Attach a rope to the low or mid pulley, hold it behind your head, and step forward facing away from it. Extend your elbows forward and up, spreading the ends at the finish, and return slowly into the stretch.
Extensión sobre la cabeza con barra Z|Seated with your back supported, keep your elbows close to your head as you lower the bar.|Sit on a bench with a backrest and hold the EZ bar overhead with a close grip. Lower it behind your head by bending your elbows and straighten your arms to raise it.
Extensión sobre la cabeza a una mano|Hold the elbow of the working arm with your other hand so it doesn't flare out.|Seated or standing, hold a dumbbell overhead with one hand. Lower the dumbbell behind your head by bending your elbow, which stays pointing up, and straighten your arm; switch arms when you finish.
Rompecráneos mancuernas|With dumbbells, each arm works on its own: lower toward the sides of your head with your palms facing each other.|Lie on a bench with a dumbbell in each hand, palms facing each other and arms straight over your chest. Lower the dumbbells toward the sides of your head by bending your elbows and straighten your arms to return.
Rompecráneos en polea|Lie with your head toward the low pulley: the cable keeps tension at the top, where a bar doesn't.|Put a bench in front of a low pulley with a short bar, lie down with your head toward the pulley, and hold the bar with your arms straight. Bend your elbows to lower the bar toward your forehead and straighten them again.
Press francés en banco inclinado|On an incline, the arm sits farther behind your body and the long head of the triceps stretches more.|Lie on a bench set at about 30° with the EZ bar overhead and your arms straight. Lower the bar behind your head by bending your elbows and straighten your arms to come up.
Extensión tríceps polea|Elbows pinned to your sides and still: only your forearms move.|Standing facing the high pulley with a straight bar or V-bar, hold it with your elbows close to your body. Push down until your arms are fully straight, squeeze your triceps, and let the bar rise until your forearms are parallel to the floor.
Extensión con cuerda|Spread the ends of the rope at the bottom and turn your hands slightly outward.|Attach a rope to the high pulley and hold it with your palms facing each other. With your elbows close to your body, push down until your arms are straight, spreading the ends of the rope, and return slowly.
Extensión tríceps unilateral|With one arm you can bring your hand slightly across your body and squeeze harder at the end.|Attach a single handle to the high pulley and hold it with one hand. With your elbow pinned to your side, push down until your arm is straight and return slowly; switch arms when the set is done.
Kickback en polea|Lean your torso forward and move your hand back until your arm is straight, with your elbow fixed at your side.|With the low pulley and a single handle, lean your torso forward and bring your elbow to your side. Extend your arm back until it's straight, squeeze your triceps, and return slowly to 90°.
Extensión agarre supino en polea|With your palms up, the medial head works more: use less weight than with the regular grip.|Grip the high pulley bar with your palms up and your elbows at your sides. Push down until your arms are straight and let the bar rise slowly without your elbows leaving your sides.
Extensión con barra V|The V-bar leaves your wrists in a natural position: push with the heel of your hand.|Attach the V-bar to the high pulley and hold it with your thumbs up. With your elbows close to your body, push until your arms are straight, squeeze, and return slowly to 90°.
Extensión en polea con banda|Tie the band to something high and push down with your elbows tucked in, just like on the cable.|Fix the band to a point above your head and hold the ends with your elbows at your sides. Extend your arms down against the resistance and return slowly until your forearms are horizontal.
Crunch en polea|On your knees, bring your elbows toward your thighs by rounding your back: don't pull with your arms.|Kneel facing the high pulley with a rope held next to your head. Flex your trunk, rounding your back and bringing your elbows toward your knees, squeeze your abs, and return slowly without sitting back on your heels.
Crunch|Come up only until your shoulder blades leave the floor and breathe out on the way up: don't pull on your neck.|Lie on your back with your knees bent and your hands at your temples or crossed on your chest. Lift your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs, hold for a second at the top, and lower slowly.
Crunch en máquina|Set the weight so you can lower slowly: the abs work on the way back too.|Sit in the crunch machine with your feet secured and grab the handles or rest your arms on the pads. Flex your trunk forward, rounding your back, and return slowly to the starting position.
Crunch con peso|Hold the plate against your chest, not behind your head, so you don't strain your neck.|Lie on your back with your knees bent and a plate or a dumbbell held against your chest. Lift your shoulders off the floor by contracting your abs and lower slowly.
Crunch en banco declinado|The decline bench lengthens the range: come up halfway and lower without letting your back rest completely.|Lie on a decline bench with your feet secured. Raise your torso, rounding your back, to the middle of the range, squeeze your abs, and lower slowly without resting your back all the way down.
Sit-up|Bring your whole torso up until you're sitting and lower under control: it's a much longer range than the crunch.|Lie on your back with your knees bent and your feet secured or planted. Raise your torso until you're sitting up, with your arms crossed on your chest, and lower slowly until you're lying down again.
Crunch bicicleta|Rotate your torso until your elbow goes toward the opposite knee, without rushing: it's the rotation that counts, not the speed.|Lie on your back with your hands at your temples and your legs raised. Bring one elbow toward the opposite knee while you extend the other leg, and alternate sides with a slow, controlled pedaling motion.
V-ups|Raise your legs and torso at the same time until you touch your feet, forming a V, and lower without dropping.|Lie on your back with your arms extended overhead and your legs straight. Raise your torso and legs together until your hands touch your feet and lower slowly to the starting position.
Crunch con balón suizo|Rest your lower back on the ball: that way the abs work from a stretched position.|Sit on a Swiss ball and walk forward until your lower back is resting on it. With your hands on your chest, raise your torso by contracting your abs and return slowly until you feel the stretch.
Elevación de piernas|Press your lower back into the floor before moving your legs, and lower them only as far as you can keep it there.|Lie on your back with your legs straight and your hands under your glutes or at your sides. Raise your legs together to vertical and lower them slowly without your lower back coming off the floor.
Crunch inverso|Bring your knees to your chest, lifting your hips off the floor: it's the hips that rise, not just the legs.|Lie on your back with your knees bent in the air. Bring your knees toward your chest, lifting your hips off the floor with your abs, and lower slowly without letting your legs drop.
Elevación de rodillas colgado|Hanging from the bar, bring your knees toward your chest without swinging your body.|Hang from a bar with your arms straight. Raise your knees toward your chest, rounding your back slightly, and lower them slowly, stopping the swing before the next rep.
Dragon flag|Keep your body rigid from shoulders to feet and lower very slowly: it's one of the toughest ab exercises there is.|Lie on a bench and grip the edge behind your head. Raise your body, resting on your shoulders, until it's almost vertical and lower it straight, like a board, as slowly as you can.
Elevación de piernas en paralelas|Supported on your forearms or with your arms straight, raise your legs with no swinging.|Support yourself on the parallel bars with your arms straight, or on the captain's chair with your forearms. Raise your straight legs to horizontal and lower them slowly.
Elevación de piernas colgado|Raise your straight legs to horizontal or higher and control the swing on every descent.|Hang from a bar with your arms straight. Raise your straight legs until they're at least parallel to the floor, hold for an instant, and lower them slowly without swinging.
Elevación de rodillas en silla romana|Get your back well supported on the pad and raise your knees without swinging your legs.|Set up in the captain's chair with your forearms on the pads and your back against the backrest. Raise your knees toward your chest by contracting your abs and lower them slowly until your legs are straight.
Plancha|Squeeze your glutes and abs as if you were about to take a punch in the stomach; breathe without letting the tension go.|Support yourself on your forearms and toes with your elbows under your shoulders. Keep your body straight from head to heels, without letting your hips sag or pike, for the set time.
Rueda abdominal|Roll out only as far as you can come back from without arching your lower back.|Kneeling or standing, hold the wheel with your hands under your shoulders. Roll forward, extending your body with a neutral back as far as you can control, and come back by contracting your abs.
Plancha lateral|Push the floor away with your forearm and lift your hips: if they drop, the obliques stop working.|Lie on your side supported on your forearm, with your elbow under your shoulder and your feet stacked. Raise your hips until your body forms a straight line and hold for the set time; repeat on the other side.
Hollow hold|Press your lower back into the floor and raise your legs and shoulders: the lower they are, the harder it is.|Lie on your back, press your lower back into the floor, and raise your shoulders and straight legs slightly, with your arms overhead. Hold the hollow position without letting your lower back come up.
Plancha con desplazamiento|Go from forearms to hands without letting your hips rock from side to side.|From the forearm plank, place one hand and then the other until your arms are straight. Lower back to your forearms one at a time and alternate the arm that leads, keeping your hips still.
Ab wheel de rodillas|On your knees the lever is shorter: it's the step before doing the rollout from standing.|Kneel on a mat with the wheel in front of you. Roll forward, extending your body and lowering your hips at the same time as far as you can control, and come back by pulling with your abs.
Plancha con arrastre de peso|Drag the weight from side to side without rotating your hips: your core fights the rotation.|In a straight-arm plank with a dumbbell or a plate at one side, reach the opposite hand under your body and drag the weight to the other side. Repeat with the other hand, keeping your hips still.
Plancha lateral con elevación de pierna|Keep your hips high while you raise the top leg: it works the obliques and the gluteus medius.|In a side plank on your forearm, with your body straight, raise the top leg about 30 cm without dropping your hips. Lower it slowly and repeat; then switch sides.
Body saw|Move forward and back from the shoulders, like a saw, without letting your hips sag.|In a forearm plank with your feet on sliders or a towel, push your body back and come forward again from your shoulders, keeping your body straight the whole time.
Clean & jerk|It's two movements: receive the bar on your shoulders, breathe, and get stable before you launch the jerk.|From the floor, lift the bar with a clean: extend your hips and knees hard and receive it on your shoulders in a squat. Stand up, dip slightly, and drive the bar overhead, receiving it in a split stance; bring your feet together with the bar locked out.
Snatch|The bar goes from the floor to overhead in one motion: the wide grip puts it at hip height when you jump.|Grip the bar very wide with your back straight. Lift it off the floor with your legs, extend your hips hard as it passes your thighs, and drop under it, receiving it with your arms locked out overhead in a deep squat. Stand up with the bar overhead.
Thruster|Use the drive out of the squat to launch the bar up: it's one continuous movement.|With the bar resting on the front of your shoulders, lower into a deep front squat. On the way up, extend your legs hard and use that drive to take the bar overhead until your arms lock out; bring it back to your shoulders as you start the next squat.
Overhead squat|Push the bar up and back the whole time: arms locked out, never relaxed.|With the bar locked out overhead and a wide grip, like a snatch grip, squat down keeping the bar over your midfoot and your chest up. Come up by pushing the floor away without letting the bar drift forward.
Power clean|Receive the bar on your shoulders in no more than a half squat: the power is in the pull.|From the floor, with your back straight, lift the bar close to your body. As it passes your knees, extend your hips, knees, and ankles explosively, shrug, and whip your elbows under to receive it on your shoulders without going below parallel.
Push press|Do a short dip and drive with your legs: the arms only finish the job.|With the bar resting on your shoulders and your elbows slightly forward, bend your knees a little, keeping your torso vertical. Extend your legs hard and use that drive to press the bar overhead until your arms lock out.
Clean pull|It's the clean without receiving the bar: finish with a full extension and a shrug.|Set up as for the clean and lift the bar off the floor with your back straight. As it passes your knees, explosively extend your hips, knees, and ankles until you're on your toes and shrug, without bending your elbows. Lower the bar under control.
Hang power snatch|Start with the bar at thigh height: without the pull from the floor, it all depends on the hip extension.|Standing with the bar hanging at thigh height and a wide grip, hinge slightly at the hips. Extend your hips explosively and drop under the bar to receive it with your arms locked out overhead, without going below parallel.
Hang power clean|From your thighs, jump with the bar and receive it on your shoulders with your elbows high.|Standing with the bar at thigh height, push your hips back slightly. Extend your hips and knees hard, shrug, and whip your elbows under the bar to receive it on your shoulders in a half squat.
Power snatch|Receive the bar overhead with your legs barely bent: you need a higher pull than in the squat snatch.|With a snatch grip, lift the bar from the floor and extend your hips hard. Receive the bar with your arms locked out overhead in a half squat, without going below parallel, and stand up.
Split jerk|Receive the bar in a split stance, front foot flat and back foot on its toes.|With the bar on your shoulders, do a short dip and drive up hard. At the same time, split your legs to get under it, lock out your arms, and bring your feet together, front foot first and then the back one.
Push jerk|After the leg drive, bend your legs again to get under the bar and receive it locked out.|With the bar on your shoulders, bend your knees slightly and drive hard. As the bar rises, bend your legs again to receive it with your arms locked out overhead and stand up.
Hang squat clean|From the thighs and received in a deep squat: it trains the speed of getting under the bar.|With the bar hanging at thigh height, extend your hips explosively and drop under it into a full front squat, receiving it on your shoulders. Stand up out of the squat with your chest up.
Dumbbell snatch|Keep the dumbbell close to your body as it rises and turn your arm under it to receive it overhead.|With a dumbbell on the floor between your feet, squat down and grab it with one hand. Extend your hips explosively and take the dumbbell overhead in one motion, with your arm locked out; lower it and alternate hands if the WOD allows it.
Dumbbell thruster|Both dumbbells on your shoulders, and the drive out of the squat launches your arms up.|With a dumbbell in each hand resting on your shoulders, lower into a deep squat. On the way up, extend your legs hard and press the dumbbells overhead until your arms lock out.
Dumbbell clean & jerk|Bring the dumbbells to your shoulders in one go and press with a leg drive.|With the dumbbells at the sides of your feet, clean them to your shoulders. Do a short dip and drive them overhead, receiving them with your legs slightly bent or in a split stance.
Muscle snatch|Without dropping under the bar: you pull it and turn it over overhead with your arms, without bending your legs.|With a snatch grip, lift the bar from the floor or your thighs with a full extension. Without bending your knees to receive it, pull it with your elbows high and turn it over until it's locked out overhead.
Clean|It's the full clean: receive it in a deep squat and use the bounce to stand up.|Grip the bar at shoulder width with your back straight, lift it close to your body, and extend your hips hard as it passes your knees. Drop under it into a full front squat, receive it on your shoulders with your elbows high, and stand up.
Burpees|Bring your chest to the floor and jump up with a clap overhead: every full rep counts.|Standing, squat down and put your hands on the floor, jump your feet back, and lower your chest to the floor. Push up, bring your feet back to your hands, and jump with your arms overhead.
Wall balls|Receive the ball by going straight into the squat: catching and descending are one movement.|Standing facing the wall with a medicine ball at chest height, lower into a deep squat. On the way up, throw the ball with your legs and arms to the target on the wall and receive it as you descend into the squat again. In Hyrox there are 100: decide beforehand how you'll break them up (for example, in sets of 20 to 25) and rest briefly between sets, standing and with the ball in your hands.
Kettlebell swing|The kettlebell rises from the hip snap, not from your arms: your arms only guide it.|With the kettlebell between your feet, hinge at the hips, grab it with both hands, and hike it back between your legs. Extend your hips explosively to bring it up to chest height and let it swing back between your legs by pushing your hips back.
Box jump|Land softly on the box with your knees bent and step down, don't jump down.|Standing facing the box, bend your legs slightly and swing your arms back. Jump up and forward, land with both feet in the middle of the box, and extend your hips at the top before stepping down.
Double unders|Jump a little higher and spin the rope with your wrists: the rope has to pass twice on each jump.|With the rope behind your heels, jump with your feet together and your legs almost straight. Spin the rope fast with your wrists, elbows close to your body, so it passes under your feet twice on each jump.
Sit-ups|In CrossFit they're done with an AbMat and the soles of your feet together: touch the floor behind your head and then your feet in front.|Sit with the soles of your feet together and your knees out, with an AbMat under your lower back. Lie back until your hands touch the floor behind your head and sit up again until you touch your feet.
Devil press|It's a burpee with dumbbells that ends in a double snatch: keep your back straight as you lift them.|With a dumbbell in each hand, do a burpee with your hands on them. As you stand up, with the dumbbells between your feet, swing them between your legs and take them overhead in one motion.
Burpee over bar|Jump over the bar with both feet at once as soon as you get up from the burpee.|Standing sideways to a bar on the floor, do a burpee with your chest to the floor. As you come up, jump sideways over the bar with both feet and start the next rep on the other side.
Kettlebell goblet clean|Bring the kettlebell from the floor to your chest, holding it by the sides of the handle.|With the kettlebell between your feet, squat down with your back straight and grab it by the sides of the handle. Extend your hips hard and bring it up to your chest, receiving it with your elbows pointing down.
Sandbag over shoulder|Hug the bag close to your body and throw it over your shoulder with a hip extension.|Squat down facing the bag, hug it, and lift it into your lap. With your back straight, extend your hips explosively and send the bag over one shoulder; alternate shoulders on each rep.
Burpee box jump over|After the burpee, jump onto the box or over it: decide beforehand whether you step on top or clear it in one jump.|Do a burpee facing the box, get up, and jump onto the box or over it, landing on the other side. Turn around and repeat from that side.
Box step-over|Step up with one foot, cross to the other side, and step down: it's the no-jump option for anyone looking after their knees.|Standing facing the box, step up with one foot and then the other until you're standing on top. Step down on the other side, turn around, and repeat, alternating the leg you step up with.
Kettlebell American swing|Take the kettlebell all the way overhead without arching your back: if you can't, do the Russian swing.|Do a kettlebell swing with the hip snap, but continue the arc until the kettlebell is overhead with your arms straight and its bottom toward the ceiling. Let it come down between your legs by pushing your hips back.
GHD sit-up|Start with few reps: the range is very long and it loads the hip flexors a lot.|Sit on the GHD with your feet secured and your hips on the pad. Lower your torso back until your hands touch the floor behind you and come up hard until you touch your feet.
GHD hip extension|Set your hips at the edge of the GHD pad and raise your torso with your glutes and hamstrings.|On the GHD, with your hips over the pad and your feet secured, lower your torso toward the floor with your back straight. Come up by extending your hips until your body is in line with your legs.
Assault bike calorías|Move your arms and legs together and find a pace you can hold: the first 10 seconds are deceiving.|Sit on the air bike with your feet on the pedals and your hands on the handles. Pedal while pushing and pulling the handles, at a steady pace, until you complete the set calories.
Remo calorías|Push with your legs, then lean your torso back, and finally pull with your arms; on the way back, the reverse.|Sit on the rower with your feet strapped in and grab the handle. Push with your legs, lean back slightly, and pull the handle toward your chest; return by straightening your arms, leaning your torso forward, and bending your legs. Repeat until you hit the set calories.
Toes to bar|Use the swing to bring your feet up until they touch the bar between your hands.|Hang from the bar with a shoulder-width grip. Swing slightly and, as your body moves back, raise your straight legs until your feet touch the bar; control the descent and link into the next swing.
Muscle-up|Pull to your hips, not just your chest, and get your shoulders over the rings with a fast turnover.|Hang from the rings with a false grip and your arms straight. Pull hard, bringing the rings toward your hips, lean your chest forward to get over them, and press until your arms are straight in support.
Rope climb|Use your feet to clamp the rope and push: your arms only hold and guide.|Grab the rope with your hands overhead and bring your knees up. Clamp the rope with your feet, push with your legs to move up, reach your hands higher, and repeat until you touch the mark; come down under control, hand over hand.
Pull-ups kipping|The swing starts at the shoulders and the drive comes from the hips: don't pull with your arms alone.|Hang with an overhand grip and build a swing, moving from chest forward to an arched back. At the right moment, extend your hips and pull until your chin clears the bar; swing back, using the momentum for the next one.
Bar muscle-up|Pull the bar toward your hips and turn your elbows over it to end up in support.|Hang from the bar, build a swing, and extend your hips hard. Pull, bringing the bar toward your hips, lean your chest over it, and press until your arms are straight in support; lower under control.
Chest to bar|Your chest has to touch the bar, not your chin: pull harder and higher.|Hang with an overhand grip and do a kipping or strict pull-up until your chest, below the collarbone, touches the bar. Lower under control and link into the next one.
Legless rope climb|No legs: climb hand over hand with your arms and your core tight.|Grab the rope with your legs hanging or in an L. Climb by alternating your hands on the rope, pulling only with your arms and back, and come down under control, hand over hand.
SkiErg 1000 m|It's the first station in Hyrox: start under control and don't burn out your arms, there are still seven to go.|Standing facing the SkiErg with your feet hip-width apart, grab the handles overhead. Pull down by bending at the hips and slightly at the knees, as if you were planting ski poles, finish with your hands next to your thighs, and stand tall again. Keep a steady pace until you reach 1000 m.
Remo 1000 m|In Hyrox it comes at the fifth station: row long and with your legs to save your arms.|With your feet strapped in, start each stroke by pushing with your legs, then lean your torso back slightly, and finish by pulling the handle toward your sternum. Return in reverse order and aim for about 26-30 strokes per minute until you complete 1000 m.
SkiErg 500 m|Half a kilometer goes at a much harder pace: keep your technique even when you're short of breath.|Grab the handles with your arms straight overhead. Pull down hard, hinging at the hips and letting your body weight drop onto the handles, finish next to your thighs, and return to the top. Hold a demanding pace until 500 m.
Remo 1000 m ritmo Hyrox|Row at the pace you'd hold in competition, knowing another kilometer of running comes next.|Set the rower's resistance to what you'd use in Hyrox and row the 1000 m at your target race pace, with the full stroke: legs, torso, and arms. When you finish, get up and start running to simulate the transition.
SkiErg 750 m|Three quarters of a kilometer: split the distance into three 250 m stretches and hold the same split on all of them.|Stand facing the SkiErg and pull the handles with your whole body, dropping your hips and finishing with your hands at your thighs. Watch the split per 500 m on the screen and try not to let it rise over the 750 m.
Remo 750 m|Use this distance to practice race pace without going to exhaustion.|Row 750 m at a sustained pace: push with your legs, lean your torso back slightly, and pull the handle toward your sternum; return arms first and legs last. Keep the split steady on the screen.
SkiErg intervalos 4x250|It's four short efforts: go out hard on each one and recover enough to repeat the same time.|Do 250 m on the SkiErg at a very high pace, rest for the set time, and repeat up to four times. Keep the hip-hinge technique on all of them and compare the time of each interval.
Sled push|Lean in with your arms straight and take short, quick steps, pushing off the balls of your feet.|Place your hands on the sled's posts with your arms almost straight and your body leaning forward. Push the sled with short, powerful steps, hips low and head in line with your back, without stopping until the mark. In Hyrox it's 50 m in four 12.5 m lengths: stop it at each line, get to the other side, and take off without pausing.
Sled pull|Pull the rope hand over hand with your body low and your feet planted: the sled shouldn't stop.|Stand in the pulling zone with the rope in front of you and the sled at the other end. With your legs bent and your torso leaning back, pull the rope hand over hand to bring the sled to you, leaving the slack rope at your side. In Hyrox it's 50 m in lengths: when the sled arrives, walk to the other side and set your feet before each pull so you don't slip.
Sled push pesado|With a lot of weight, the sled is hardest to get moving: keep your body leaning far forward and don't stop.|Load the sled above your competition weight, lean in with your arms slightly bent, and push with short, very powerful steps. Keep the tension constant so you don't have to start again from a standstill.
Sled push ligero y rápido|With little weight, the goal is speed: run behind the sled with quick strides.|Load it light, place your hands on the posts, and push the sled as fast as you can with short, frequent strides. Slow down when you reach the mark and rest before repeating.
Sled drag hacia atrás|Walk backward with short steps and your knees bent: the quads work with no impact.|Hold handles or a rope attached to the sled and walk backward with your knees bent, your torso upright, and your arms straight. Take short, continuous steps without letting the sled stop.
Burpee broad jump|Bring your chest to the floor and jump forward as far as you can with both feet at once.|Do a burpee, lowering your chest to the floor, and as you get up, jump forward with both feet at once. Land softly, go straight down into the next burpee, and keep moving forward until the set distance. In Hyrox it's 80 m: find a pace you can hold without stopping.
Farmers carry|Shoulders down and back, abs tight, and short steps: don't let the weights swing you.|Grab a heavy dumbbell or kettlebell in each hand and stand up with your back straight. Walk with short, quick steps, arms straight at your sides and torso upright, for the set distance or time. In Hyrox it's 200 m with two kettlebells: squeeze your grip from the first step and, if you have to put them down, do it under control and get going again right away.
Sandbag lunges|Rest the bag on your shoulders, behind your neck, and keep your torso upright on every lunge.|Place the bag on your upper back or shoulders. Step forward into a lunge, lowering your back knee until it gently touches the floor, and come up to take the next one with the other leg.
Sandbag clean|Hug the bag from the floor and bring it to your chest with a hip snap, not with your back.|Squat down facing the bag with your back straight, grab it from underneath, and lift it to your thighs. Extend your hips hard and receive it at your chest, hugging it, standing tall. Put it down on the floor and repeat.
Lunges con sandbag 100 m|In Hyrox the back knee has to touch the floor on every lunge: don't shorten your steps.|With the bag on your shoulders, move forward in lunges, touching the floor with your back knee on each one, until you complete 100 m. Keep the bag stable and your torso upright even as your legs tire.
Farmers carry con kettlebell|Hold the kettlebells by the middle of the handle so they don't tip forward as you walk.|Grab a kettlebell in each hand by the middle of the handle and stand up with your chest high. Walk with short, controlled steps, without letting the bells hit your legs, for the set distance.
Sandbag carry al hombro|Switch the bag to the other shoulder on each length so you don't always load the same side.|Lift the bag onto one shoulder and hold it with both hands. Walk with your torso straight, without leaning to the opposite side, and switch shoulders halfway through the distance.
Sandbag squat|Hug the bag against your chest and squat down with your torso very upright.|Hold the bag in a bear hug in front of your chest. Squat until your thighs are parallel with your elbows inside your knees and come up by pushing the floor away with your whole foot.
Bear hug carry|Hug the bag or stone tight to your chest and breathe high: your abs stay braced.|Lift the bag or stone off the floor and hug it against your chest with your forearms underneath. Walk with short steps and your back straight for the set distance without letting it slip.
Turkish get-up|Keep your eyes on the kettlebell for the whole exercise and don't let the top arm bend.|Lie down with the kettlebell in one hand and your arm straight toward the ceiling. Step by step, prop yourself on your elbow, then on your hand, lift your hips, sweep your leg under until you're kneeling, and stand up. Reverse the steps in order until you're back on the floor.
Goblet squat|Hold the kettlebell by the sides of the handle against your chest and lower between your legs.|Standing with your feet slightly wider than your shoulders, hold the kettlebell by the sides of the handle at chest height. Squat down with your torso upright to the deepest position you can control and come up by pushing with your whole foot.
Kettlebell snatch|Punch your hand through the handle just before the kettlebell reaches the top so it doesn't bang your forearm.|With the kettlebell between your feet, do a one-arm swing and, instead of letting it float forward, pull it up close to your body. At the end, punch your hand through the handle and lock out your arm overhead; let it come down between your legs.
Sentadilla goblet con pausa|Pause for three seconds at the bottom with your elbows inside your knees and your chest up.|Hold the kettlebell against your chest and squat down to full depth. Stay still for three seconds with your back straight and come up by pushing the floor away.
Kettlebell clean y press|Clean the kettlebell to the rack and press it overhead without arching your back.|With the kettlebell between your feet, do a one-arm clean to the rack position, with the bell on your forearm. From there, squeeze your glutes and abs and press until your arm locks out; lower it to the rack and then between your legs.
Swing a una mano|With one hand, your core works against rotation: don't let your shoulders turn toward the kettlebell.|Hold the kettlebell with one hand and hike it between your legs by pushing your hips back. Extend your hips explosively to bring it up to chest height and let it come back with your arm relaxed; switch hands when you finish.
Kettlebell windmill|Keep your eyes on the kettlebell overhead and lower by sliding your other hand down your leg, without bending the top arm.|With the kettlebell locked out overhead and your feet turned toward the opposite side, push your hips toward the side of the top arm. Slide your other hand down the inside of your leg as far as you can reach and come up slowly.
Kettlebell halo|Circle the kettlebell around your head close to your neck, with your abs tight and without arching.|Standing or kneeling, hold the kettlebell upside down by the sides of the handle in front of your chest. Take it around your head, passing close to the back of your neck, and return to the front; alternate directions.
Kettlebell clean|The kettlebell should roll around your hand and land softly on your forearm, without banging it.|From the swing position, pull the kettlebell up close to your body and turn your hand through the handle to receive it in the rack position, with your elbow at your side. Lower it between your legs again.
Kettlebell racked carry|Walk with the kettlebells at your shoulders and your elbows tucked in: it's core and posture work.|Bring one or two kettlebells to the rack position, with the bell resting on your forearm. Walk with short steps, chest up and abs tight, without leaning to either side, for the set distance.
Bear crawl|Crawl on all fours with your knees a hand's width off the floor and your back flat.|On all fours, lift your knees a few centimeters off the floor. Move forward by moving the opposite hand and foot together, with short steps, your back flat, and your hips at shoulder height.
Dead bug|Press your lower back into the floor and extend the opposite arm and leg very slowly.|Lie on your back with your arms straight toward the ceiling and your knees at 90°. Extend one arm back and the opposite leg forward without your lower back coming off the floor, return, and alternate.
Mountain climbers|Drive your knees to your chest, alternating fast, without your hips rising or dropping.|In a straight-arm plank, bring one knee toward your chest and switch legs quickly, as if running in place, keeping your shoulders over your hands.
Pallof press|Press the handle straight out and hold: the cable tries to rotate you and your core won't let it.|Standing sideways to a pulley set at chest height, hold the handle with both hands at your sternum. Extend your arms forward without letting your torso rotate toward the pulley, hold for two seconds, and return to your chest.
Plancha con toque de hombro|Set your feet a little wider for more stability and tap the opposite shoulder without rocking your hips.|In a straight-arm plank, lift one hand and tap the opposite shoulder. Put it back down and repeat with the other hand, keeping your hips still and your body straight.
Bird dog|Extend the opposite arm and leg to horizontal without rotating your hips: as if you had a glass of water on your back.|On all fours with your hands under your shoulders and your knees under your hips, extend one arm forward and the opposite leg back at the same time. Hold for two seconds and return; alternate sides.
Hollow rock|Hold the hollow position and rock like a rocking chair without breaking it.|From the hollow hold, with your lower back pressed down and your arms and legs straight, rock forward and back, keeping your body rigid in a banana shape.
Inchworm|Walk your hands out to a plank and come back with short steps: it stretches the hamstrings and wakes up the shoulders.|Standing, bend at the hips and put your hands on the floor with your legs as straight as possible. Walk your hands forward to a plank and come back by walking your feet toward your hands.
Crab walk|Lift your hips and walk on your hands and feet, with your belly facing the ceiling.|Sit with your hands on the floor behind you and your feet in front, and lift your hips off the floor. Walk forward or backward, moving the opposite hand and foot, without letting your hips drop.
Sprawl|Jump your feet back and drop your hips to the floor, with no push-up: then get back up fast.|Standing, put your hands on the floor and shoot your feet back until your hips are close to the floor. Jump your feet back to your hands and stand up quickly.
Battle ropes|Move the ropes with your whole body, with your knees bent and your abs tight.|Hold one end of the rope in each hand and get into a half squat. Make waves, alternating your arms or both together, fast and continuously, without letting the ropes go still.
Medicine ball slam|Slam the ball into the floor with your whole body and pick it up by squatting with your back straight.|Hold the ball overhead with your arms straight. Slam it hard into the floor, bending your hips and knees, pick it up with your back straight, and repeat.
Sentadilla con salto|Lower into a half squat and jump as high as you can; land softly and go straight into the next one.|Standing with your feet shoulder-width apart, lower into a squat and jump up hard, extending your hips and knees. Land with your knees bent and go straight down into the next jump.
Salto lateral|Jump from side to side with both feet together and land on the balls of your feet.|Standing next to a line or a low obstacle, jump sideways over it with your feet together and jump back to the other side. Keep the jumps quick and cushioned.
Skater jump|Jump sideways on one foot like a speed skater and hold the landing for an instant.|Standing on one leg, jump to the opposite side and land on the other leg, sweeping the trailing leg behind the standing one. Balance for an instant and jump back.
Lanzamiento de balón medicinal|Throw the ball forward or up with a full extension of your legs and hips.|Hold the ball at chest height, lower into a half squat, and extend your legs hard, throwing it forward or up as far as possible. Pick it up and repeat.
Lanzamiento rotacional de balón|The power comes from the hip turn: your arms only pass the drive on to the wall.|Standing sideways to a wall with the ball at hip height, rotate your torso back and throw the ball against the wall by turning your hips hard. Catch it and repeat; switch sides.
Volteo de neumático|Drive with your legs and hips, don't pull with your back: the tire comes up like a deadlift.|Squat down facing the tire with your chest against it and your hands underneath. Drive with your legs to lift it, extend your hips, and when it's standing up, push it with your hands to flip it.
TRX remo|Walk your feet toward the anchor point to make it harder; move them away to make it easier.|Hold the TRX handles with your arms straight and your body leaning back, straight from heels to head. Pull by driving your elbows back and your chest toward your hands, squeeze your shoulder blades, and lower slowly.
Landmine press|Press with both hands from your chest and follow through with your legs: it's a whole-body push.|Hold the end of the bar with both hands at chest height, with one foot forward. Extend your arms forward and up along the arc of the bar, pushing the floor away with your back leg, and return to your chest under control.
Pasos laterales con banda|Keep tension on the band at all times: your feet never come together.|Put a mini band above your knees or around your ankles and lower into a half squat. Take short side steps, keeping the tension, without bringing your feet together, and come back the other way.
Zancada lateral|Sit your hips back over the bending leg and keep the other one straight with the foot flat.|Standing with a dumbbell in your hands or no weight, take a wide step to one side and lower by bending that knee while the other leg stays straight. Push off the bent leg to return to the center and alternate sides.
Cargada de mochila|Fill the backpack with weight and bring it from the floor to your chest with your back straight, like a sandbag.|With a loaded backpack on the floor, squat down with your back straight and grab it by the straps or from underneath. Bring it up to your chest with a hip snap, hugging it, and put it back on the floor under control.
TRX flexiones|With your feet in the straps, your body tends to sag: brace your abs like in a plank.|Put your feet in the TRX foot cradles and your hands on the floor under your shoulders. Lower your chest toward the floor with your body straight and press until your arms are straight, without letting your legs swing.
TRX sentadilla|Hold the handles to sit your hips back and go lower than you could without help.|Facing the anchor point, hold the handles with your arms straight. Squat down by sitting your hips back, using the straps to keep your torso upright, and come up by driving with your legs.
TRX fondos|With your arms close to your body and the straps at your sides, lower only to 90° at the elbow.|Facing away from the anchor point, hold the handles at the sides of your hips with your arms straight and your feet in front of you. Lower by bending your elbows to about 90° and press until they're straight again.
TRX curl|Lean back with your arms straight and pull only by bending your elbows toward your forehead.|Hold the handles with your palms up and your body leaning back. Bend your elbows, bringing your hands toward your forehead without moving your elbows out of place, and straighten your arms slowly.
Remo con banda de pie|With one leg forward and the band at waist height, pull with one arm and let your torso rotate a little.|Anchor the band at waist height and face it with one leg forward. Pull with one arm, driving your elbow back close to your body and rotating your torso slightly, return slowly, and alternate arms.
Press con banda de pie|Anchor the band behind you at chest height and press forward without your hips moving.|Facing away from the anchor, with one foot forward and the band running under your arms, hold the ends at chest height. Press forward until your arms are straight and return slowly, resisting the pull.
Zancada con rotación torácica|Rotate from your upper back: the hand on the floor and your front leg stay put while the other arm rises.|Standing, take a long step forward with your left leg and lower into a lunge, with your back foot on its toes. Lean your torso forward and place your right hand on the floor inside your front foot, with your left hand on your knee. Rotate your torso to the left and raise that arm straight toward the ceiling, following it with your eyes; lower it, stand back up, and repeat with the other leg.
Rodilla al pecho con alcance|Rise onto the toes of your standing leg as you hug your knee: you stretch the glute on one side and work the calf and your balance on the other.|Standing, lift your left knee and hug it with both hands just below it, pulling it toward your chest as you rise onto the toes of your right foot. Let go, set your foot down next to the other, and reach both arms overhead as you rise onto your toes. Lower your heels and repeat with the other leg.
Talón al glúteo con alcance|Keep your knee pointing at the floor and next to the other one: if it drifts forward, the quad stops stretching.|Standing, bend your left knee and grab the top of your foot behind you with your left hand, pulling your heel toward your glute. At the same time, reach your right arm toward the ceiling and rise onto the toes of your right foot. Hold for a moment, let go of your foot, set it down, and repeat with the other leg.
Carrera continua|Run at a pace where you can talk in short sentences: sustainable, not entirely comfortable.|Run at a steady pace for the set time, with short strides and a high cadence, about 165-180 steps per minute. Keep your torso upright, your arms relaxed, and your breathing even.
Intervalos 400 m|Each 400 m at your best 3-5 km pace: the rest between reps matters as much as the rep.|Warm up with 10 minutes of jogging and run 400 m repeats at a hard, steady pace, with 60-90 s of jogging or walking recovery between them. Try to hit the same time on all of them.
Series 1 km|Start at a pace you can repeat on every rep, not the one you happen to hit on the first.|After your warm-up, run 1 km at 5-10 km race pace and recover with 2-3 minutes of jogging. Repeat for the set number of reps, trying to make the last one as fast as the first.
Tempo run|Tempo is a comfortably hard pace: you can say three or four words, not a whole sentence.|Warm up for 10 minutes and run 15 to 30 minutes at threshold pace, roughly what you could hold for an hour in a race. Finish with an easy cool-down jog.
Cuestas|Run up with short strides, landing on the balls of your feet, and with active arms.|Find a 5-8% hill and run up hard for 30-90 seconds. Walk or jog down easy to recover and repeat for the set number of reps.
Fartlek|Play with the pace with no stopwatch: speed up to one lamppost, recover to the next.|Run at an easy pace and mix in pace changes of different lengths, from 20 seconds to 3 minutes, depending on the terrain or how you feel. Go back to an easy jog between surges.
Rodaje suave zona 2|In zone 2 you should be able to breathe through your nose only: if you're panting, slow down even if it feels slow.|Run at a very easy intensity, around 60-70% of your max heart rate, for the set time. The goal is to rack up minutes with little fatigue, not to go fast.
Carrera por tempo|Split the time into blocks at threshold pace with 1-2 minutes of jogging between them.|After warming up, run blocks of 5 to 10 minutes at threshold pace with short jog recoveries between them, for example 3 × 8 minutes. Finish with a few easy minutes.
Series 800 m|Eight hundred meters call for a slightly slower pace than 400s: control the first lap.|Warm up and run 800 m repeats at your 5 km pace, with 90 seconds to 2 minutes of recovery between them. Check your time on each 400 m lap so you don't go out too fast.
Series 200 m|They're almost sprints: run fast but relaxed, without clenching your jaw or shoulders.|After a good warm-up, run 200 m very fast with good form and recover by walking or jogging 200 m. Repeat for the set number of reps, holding your speed.
Rodaje largo|The long run is run slow: distance is the goal, not pace.|Run at an easy, steady pace for the set time, the longest of the week. Carry water if it lasts over an hour, and don't pick up the pace at the end even if you feel good.
Progresivos|Start easy and speed up little by little until you finish at a hard pace, short of a sprint.|Run 80-100 m stretches, starting at a jog and gradually picking up the pace to the end. Walk back and repeat; they can also be done at the end of an easy run.
Trote en cinta|On the treadmill, set a 1% incline to mimic the effort of running outside.|Set the treadmill to an easy jogging speed and a 1% incline. Run with short, relaxed strides, without holding on, for the set time.
Cuestas en cinta|Raise the incline on each rep and drop it all the way to recover: the treadmill gives you an exact hill.|After warming up, set the treadmill to a 6-10% incline and run hard for 1-2 minutes. Lower the incline and speed to recover by walking for the same time, and repeat.
Remo ergómetro|The stroke is 60% legs, 20% torso, and 20% arms: don't pull with your arms before you push.|Sit on the rower with your feet strapped in and grab the handle. Push with your legs, lean your torso back slightly, and pull the handle toward your sternum; return by straightening your arms first and then bending your legs.
Bicicleta|Set the saddle so your knee is almost straight at the bottom: a low saddle loads the knees.|Set the saddle at hip height and sit with your feet on the pedals. Pedal at the set cadence and resistance, with your torso relaxed and your knees in line with your feet.
Elíptica|Push and pull the machine's arms: that way your legs, arms, and back all work.|Step onto the elliptical, grab the moving handles, and pedal with your feet flat on the platforms. Keep your torso upright and a steady pace, pushing and pulling the handles.
Intervalos HIIT en bici|The intervals really are all-out: if you can talk during the effort, raise the resistance.|Warm up for 5 minutes and alternate very intense 20-40 second efforts with 1-2 minutes of easy pedaling. Repeat for the set number of intervals and finish with a few easy minutes.
Ski erg intervalos|Do sets of 30 seconds to a minute with your whole body, with rests of the same length.|On the SkiErg, alternate hard 30-60 second efforts with the same time of easy recovery or rest. Keep the hip hinge on every pull even when fatigue sets in.
Escaladora|Don't lean on the rails: your body weight should be on your legs.|Step onto the stair climber and set a pace you can hold. Climb the steps planting your whole foot, with your torso upright and your hands barely touching the rails for balance.
Remo 2000 m|It's the classic rowing test: go out at a controlled pace for the first 500 m and push on the last 500.|Row 2000 m with the full stroke: legs, torso, and arms. Set a target split per 500 m, hold it through the middle, and speed up on the final stretch.
Bicicleta zona 2|Pedal at a pace that lets you hold a conversation without breaks: it's your aerobic base.|Set a moderate resistance and pedal at an easy, steady pace, around 60-70% of your max heart rate, for the set time.
Bicicleta Tabata|It's 8 rounds of 20 seconds all-out and 10 of rest: 4 minutes that feel very long.|After warming up, pedal for 20 seconds at maximum intensity with high resistance and rest for 10 seconds pedaling very easy. Repeat eight times in a row.
Assault bike intervalos|Arms and legs together: start hard and keep your RPM up through the whole interval.|On the air bike, alternate short, intense efforts of 15-30 seconds with longer rests of easy pedaling. Push and pull the handles together on each effort.
Remo zona 2|Row easy and long, at about 20-22 strokes per minute, without tiring your arms.|Row at low intensity for the set time, with the full stroke and a relaxed rhythm. You should be able to talk in full sentences while you row.
Remo 500 m intervalos|Five hundred hard meters with half or the same time of recovery: aim for even splits.|Row 500 m at an intense pace, recover for 1-2 minutes rowing easy or resting, and repeat for the set number of reps. Keep the legs-torso-arms technique even when fatigue sets in.
Ciclismo en carretera|Drink and eat something if the ride goes over an hour, and always wear a helmet.|Head out on the road bike at the set intensity and time, with a cadence of 80-90 RPM. Shift gears on the climbs to keep your cadence instead of mashing the pedals.
Press banca declinado|The decline shortens the range and loads the lower chest: bring the bar down to the bottom of your sternum.|Lie on a decline bench with your feet secured and grip the bar slightly wider than your shoulders. Unrack it, lower it to your lower chest, and press until your arms are straight.
Press declinado mancuernas|Ask for help getting the dumbbells into position on the decline, or kick them up from your thighs before lying back.|Lie on the decline bench with your feet secured and a dumbbell in each hand over your lower chest. Lower them with your elbows at about 45° to chest height and press up, bringing them slightly together.
Press declinado en Smith|In the Smith machine you can load the decline more safely: set the bench so the bar lands at the bottom of your sternum.|Put a decline bench inside the Smith machine and lie down with your feet secured. Unlock the bar, lower it to your lower chest under control, and press until your arms are straight.
Press declinado en máquina|The decline machine follows a path down and forward: push in that direction.|Set the seat so the handles come out level with the bottom of your sternum. With your back and head supported, extend your elbows, moving the handles forward and slightly toward your feet, squeeze your chest, and let them come back under control.
Press declinado en polea|With the pulleys high, press down and forward, bringing your hands together at belly-button height.|Set the pulleys high and stand in the middle with a handle in each hand at chest height. Press forward and down until your hands almost meet and return slowly.
Pullover mancuerna|Take the dumbbell behind your head with your elbows slightly bent and feel the stretch in your chest and lats.|Lie on a bench with a dumbbell held in both hands over your chest. Lower it in an arc behind your head with your elbows slightly bent until you feel the stretch and return along the same path.
Pullover con barra Z|With the EZ bar held on the curves, lower behind your head without flaring your elbows.|Lie on a flat bench with the EZ bar over your chest and your arms almost straight. Take it in an arc behind your head until you feel the stretch and bring it back up over your chest.
Pullover en polea|With your arms almost straight, bring the bar down in an arc to your thighs, pulling with your lats.|Standing facing the high pulley with a straight bar or a rope, lean your torso forward slightly and hold the attachment with your arms straight. Pull down in an arc to your thighs without bending your elbows any further and return slowly to the top, into the stretch.
Pullover máquina|Rest your elbows on the pads and push with them, not with your hands.|Sit in the pullover machine with your back against the pad and your elbows on the pads. Drive your elbows down and forward in an arc to your sides and return slowly to the stretch overhead.
Jalón con brazos rectos con cuerda|With the rope you can take your hands farther back past your hips and spread them at the end.|Attach a rope to the high pulley and hold it with your arms straight. Lean forward slightly and pull the rope down in an arc to the sides of your hips, spreading the ends at the finish, and return slowly.
Encogimientos|Raise your shoulders straight up toward your ears, without rolling them, and hold for a second at the top.|Standing with the bar hanging in front of your thighs and a shoulder-width grip, raise your shoulders toward your ears as high as you can. Hold for a second and lower slowly until your traps are stretched.
Encogimientos con mancuernas|With the dumbbells at your sides, the path is more natural than with a bar: get a good stretch at the bottom.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand at your sides, raise your shoulders toward your ears without bending your elbows. Squeeze at the top for a second and lower slowly.
Encogimientos en Smith|The guide rails let you go heavy without worrying about balance: keep your arms straight.|Stand facing the Smith bar at thigh height and grip it overhand. Unlock it, raise your shoulders toward your ears, squeeze, and lower slowly.
Encogimientos en máquina|Get your shoulders under the pads and raise straight up without letting your head jut forward.|Set the machine with the pads on your shoulders or grab the handles at your sides. Raise your shoulders as high as possible, hold for an instant, and lower slowly into the stretch.
Encogimientos en polea|The cable pulls from below with constant tension: raise your shoulders without bending your elbows.|Stand between two low pulleys, or facing one with a bar, and hold the handles with your arms straight. Raise your shoulders toward your ears, hold for a second, and lower slowly.
Encogimientos con barra hexagonal|Inside the trap bar, the weight sits at your sides: you can load more without it rubbing your legs.|Step inside the trap bar and grab the handles with your palms facing each other. Lift it until you're standing and, with your arms straight, raise your shoulders toward your ears; lower slowly.
Retracción escapular en polea|Only the shoulder blades move: the arms stay straight and pull back without bending the elbows.|Seated at the low pulley with your arms straight and the handle in your hands, squeeze your shoulder blades together by pulling your shoulders back without bending your elbows. Hold for a second and let them spread apart again.
Pull-apart con banda|Pull the band apart with straight arms until it touches your chest: the rhomboids and rear delts do the work.|Hold the band with your arms straight in front of you at shoulder height and your hands shoulder-width apart. Pull it apart by opening your arms out to the sides until it touches your chest, squeeze your shoulder blades together, and return slowly.
Scap pull-ups|Hanging with straight arms, raise your body a few centimeters just by pulling your shoulder blades down.|Hang from the bar with your arms straight and your body relaxed. Without bending your elbows, pull your shoulder blades down and together to raise your body a few centimeters, hold for an instant, and relax again.
Elevaciones frontales|Raise only to eye level: any higher and the traps take over from the front delts.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand in front of your thighs, raise your arms forward with your elbows slightly bent to shoulder or eye height. Lower slowly without swinging your torso.
Elevaciones frontales con disco|Hold the plate by its sides, like a steering wheel, and raise it without arching your back.|Standing, hold a plate with both hands by its sides in front of your thighs. Raise it forward with your arms almost straight to eye level and lower it slowly.
Elevaciones frontales con barra|With the bar, both arms rise together: use a shoulder-width grip and light weight.|Standing with the bar in front of your thighs and your palms down, raise it forward with your arms almost straight to shoulder height. Lower it under control without letting it swing you.
Elevaciones frontales en polea|Facing away from the low pulley, the cable pulls from behind and the tension doesn't disappear at the bottom.|Set the pulley low with a single handle and face away from it with the cable between your legs. Raise your arm forward to shoulder height and lower it slowly; switch arms when you finish.
Elevaciones frontales con cuerda|Raise the rope with both hands and your thumbs up: the neutral grip is easier on the shoulders.|Facing away from the low pulley, hold the rope with both hands between your legs and a neutral grip. Raise your arms forward to shoulder height and lower them slowly.
Elevaciones frontales alternas|Alternate arms without your torso leaning back: every rep comes out clean.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand, raise one arm forward to shoulder height while the other stays down. Lower it slowly and raise the other.
Remo al mentón|Lead with your elbows above your hands, and don't go past chest height if your shoulders bother you.|Standing with the bar in front of your thighs and a grip slightly narrower than your shoulders, pull up, driving your elbows out to the sides and above your hands. Raise it to your lower chest and lower slowly.
Remo al mentón con mancuernas|With dumbbells, each arm follows its own path: it's the most comfortable version for the shoulders.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand in front of your thighs, pull up, driving your elbows out and above your hands to chest height. Lower under control.
Remo al mentón con barra Z|The EZ bar leaves your wrists slightly turned and takes the strain off them.|Hold the EZ bar on the middle curves with your palms toward you. Pull up, driving your elbows out to the sides until the bar reaches your lower chest, and lower it slowly.
Remo al mentón con cuerda en polea|The rope lets you spread your hands at the top: pull your elbows out and up.|Attach a rope to the low pulley and hold it with your hands together. Pull up, spreading the ends and driving your elbows above your hands to chest height, and lower slowly.
Remo al mentón agarre ancho|With your hands wider, the side delts work more and the traps less.|Grip the bar quite a bit wider than your shoulders. Pull up, driving your elbows out to the sides until the bar reaches belly-button or chest height, and lower it slowly.
Curl alterno mancuernas|Turn your palm up as you curl and alternate arms without swinging your torso.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand and your palms facing your body, curl one while rotating your wrist until your palm faces your shoulder. Lower it slowly and repeat with the other arm.
Curl en banco inclinado|With your arms hanging behind your body, the biceps start in a deep stretch: don't let your elbows move forward.|Sit on a bench set at 45-60° with a dumbbell in each hand and your arms hanging. Curl the dumbbells by bending your elbows without moving them forward and lower them slowly until your arms are fully straight.
Curl concentrado|Rest your elbow on the inside of your thigh and curl slowly: there's no way to cheat.|Sitting on a bench with your legs apart, rest your elbow on your inner thigh with a dumbbell in your hand. Curl the dumbbell toward your shoulder, squeeze your biceps, and lower it slowly.
Curl Zottman|Curl up with your palms up, turn them down at the very top, and lower slowly with an overhand grip.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand and your palms forward, do a regular curl on the way up. At the top, rotate your wrists until your palms face down and lower like that, slowly, to work the forearms too.
Curl con mancuernas|Curl both dumbbells together, turning your wrists slightly outward at the end.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand at your sides and your palms forward, bend your elbows to curl both dumbbells up to your shoulders. Squeeze at the top and lower slowly.
Curl con mancuernas a 45°|Open your arms about 45° from your body as you curl: it changes the angle and works the short head more.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand, move your arms about 45° out from your torso with your palms forward. Curl the dumbbells by bending your elbows in that direction and lower them slowly.
Curl con supinación completa|Start with your palms facing in and finish with your pinky higher than your thumb.|With the dumbbells at your sides and a neutral grip, curl while gradually rotating your wrists until your palms face up and slightly out. Lower, reversing the rotation.
Drag curl|Drag the dumbbell up along your body, driving your elbows back, not forward.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand, bring them up close to your torso while your elbows travel back, as if you were dragging the dumbbells up your body. Lower along the same path.
Curl con mancuernas sentado|Seated, you take away the leg drive: the biceps do all the work.|Sit on the edge of a bench with your back straight and a dumbbell in each hand. Curl the dumbbells with your palms up and your elbows still, and lower them slowly.
Curl en polea|The cable keeps tension at the top of the curl, where a dumbbell loses its load.|Standing facing the low pulley with a straight bar or EZ bar, hold it with your palms up and your elbows close to your body. Curl up to your chest, squeeze, and lower slowly.
Curl Bayesian|Facing away from the pulley, the arm sits behind your body and the biceps work in a stretch.|Face away from a low pulley with a single handle and step forward, leaving your arm straight behind your body. Bend your elbow, bringing your hand toward your shoulder without letting the elbow move forward, and return slowly.
Curl en polea con cuerda|Turn your wrists outward as you curl, pinkies up: the biceps work more than with a fixed neutral grip.|Step back from the low pulley so the cable doesn't rub your legs and hold the rope by the knots. As you bend your elbows, rotate your wrists outward and spread the ends, squeeze for a second with your biceps contracted, and straighten your arms all the way again.
Curl en polea alta|With your arms out at shoulder height, bring your hands toward your ears.|Stand between two high pulleys with a handle in each hand and your arms straight out to the sides. Bend your elbows, bringing your hands toward your head without dropping your elbows, squeeze, and return slowly.
Curl en polea a una mano|Work each arm separately and turn your palm slightly outward at the end.|Standing next to a low pulley with a single handle, bend your elbow to bring your hand toward your shoulder with your elbow close to your body. Lower slowly and switch arms after the set.
Curl en polea tumbado|Lying on your back with the pulley at your feet, your back can't help.|Lie on the floor or a bench with your feet toward a low pulley and hold a bar with your arms straight. Curl the bar toward your chest by bending your elbows, which stay against the floor or your body, and return slowly.
Press cerrado|Grip the bar at shoulder width, no closer, and lower with your elbows tucked in to your body.|Lie on the bench and grip the bar with your hands shoulder-width apart. Lower it to your lower chest with your elbows close to your torso and press until your arms are straight, loading mostly the triceps.
Fondos en banco|Keep your back close to the bench and lower only to 90° at the elbow to look after your shoulders.|Place your hands on the edge of a bench behind you and your legs straight or bent in front. Lower by bending your elbows, which point back, to about 90° and press until your arms are straight.
Press JM|It's a cross between the close-grip press and the French press: lower the bar toward your neck by bending your elbows and shoulders.|Lie down holding the bar with a close grip and your arms straight. Lower the bar toward your chin or upper chest, letting your elbows travel slightly forward, and press until your arms are straight.
Fondos en paralelas|Torso upright and elbows back: that way dips work mostly the triceps.|Support yourself on the parallel bars with your arms straight and your torso vertical. Lower by bending your elbows, which go back and stay close to your body, to about 90°, and press until your arms are straight.
Press cerrado mancuernas|Hold the dumbbells together over your chest with your palms facing each other and lower with your elbows tucked in.|Lie on a bench with two dumbbells together over your chest and a neutral grip. Lower them until they touch your chest with your elbows close to your body and press until your arms are straight.
Press cerrado en Smith|The Smith machine lets you push the triceps to the limit without worrying about balancing the bar.|Lie on a bench inside the Smith machine and grip the bar at shoulder width. Unlock it, lower it to your lower chest with your elbows tucked in, and press until your arms are straight.
Flexiones diamante|Bring your hands together under your chest, forming a diamond with your thumbs and index fingers.|In the push-up position, bring your hands together under your chest with your thumbs and index fingers touching. Lower your chest toward your hands with your elbows close to your body and press until your arms are straight.
Fondos en banco con lastre|Have someone place the plate on your thighs and lower under control: the weight pushes you down.|With your hands on a bench behind you, your legs straight on another bench, and a plate on your thighs, lower by bending your elbows to 90° and press until your arms are straight.
Press cerrado con barra Z|The EZ bar leaves your wrists in a more natural position on the close grip.|Lie on the bench and hold the EZ bar on the middle curves. Lower it to your lower chest with your elbows close to your body and press until your arms are straight.
Patada de tríceps|Pin your upper arm to your side, parallel to the floor, and extend your elbow until your arm is straight.|Put one hand and one knee on a bench and hold a dumbbell in the other hand, with your upper arm against your body and your elbow at 90°. Extend your elbow, moving the dumbbell back until your arm is straight, and return slowly.
Patada de tríceps a dos manos|Bent over with both arms at once, squeeze hard at the top without letting your elbows drop.|Standing with your torso bent forward and a dumbbell in each hand, pin your upper arms to your body with your elbows at 90°. Extend both elbows back at the same time, squeeze, and return slowly.
Patada de tríceps con banda|Step on the band in front of you and extend your arm back against the resistance, which grows at the end.|Step on one end of the band with your front foot and hold the other end with your torso bent forward and your elbow close to your body. Extend your arm back until it's straight and return slowly.
Curl de muñeca|Rest your forearms on your thighs or a bench and let the bar roll down to your fingers.|Seated, rest your forearms on your thighs with your palms up and your wrists past your knees. Let the bar roll down to your fingers, close them, and curl your wrists up as far as possible.
Curl de muñeca con mancuerna|With a dumbbell you work each forearm separately: raise and lower your wrist slowly.|Seated, rest one forearm on your thigh with your palm up and a dumbbell in your hand. Curl your wrist to raise the dumbbell and lower it until you feel the stretch.
Curl de muñeca en polea|The low pulley gives constant tension through the wrist's whole range.|Standing or kneeling in front of a low pulley with a short bar, rest your forearms on a bench with your palms up. Curl your wrists to raise the bar and lower it slowly.
Curl de muñeca tras la espalda|With the bar behind your glutes and your palms facing back, only your wrists move.|Standing, hold a bar behind your body with your palms facing back and your arms straight. Curl your wrists to raise the bar toward your glutes and lower it slowly.
Curl inverso|With your palms down, the brachioradialis does the work: use less weight than in the regular curl.|Standing with an EZ bar or straight bar and your palms down, bend your elbows to raise the bar to your chest without moving your elbows. Lower it slowly until your arms are straight.
Curl inverso en polea|The cable keeps the forearm under tension at the top: keep your wrists straight.|Facing a low pulley with a straight bar, hold it with your palms down. Raise the bar by bending your elbows up to your chest and lower it slowly with your wrists firm.
Curl inverso con mancuernas|With dumbbells you can go one at a time and watch that your wrist doesn't bend.|With a dumbbell in each hand and your palms down, bend your elbows to raise the dumbbells to your chest. Lower them slowly, keeping your wrists in line with your forearms.
Colgado de barra|Hang with your shoulders active, pulled slightly down, instead of hanging loose from your joints.|Grab a bar with your hands shoulder-width apart and hang with your feet off the floor. Hold the position for the set time with your arms straight and your shoulders slightly active.
Rodillo de muñeca|Wind up the cord by turning your wrists, never with your arms: go up and down slowly.|Hold the roller with your arms straight in front of you at shoulder height, with the weight hanging from the cord. Turn your wrists alternately to wind up the cord until the weight reaches the top and unwind it slowly.
Pinza con discos|Put two smooth plates together, smooth sides out, and hold them with your fingers only: it's pure pinch strength.|Put two plates together with the smooth sides facing out and grab them with one hand, fingers on one side and thumb on the other. Lift them off the floor and hold them, standing, for the set time; switch hands.
Colgado con toalla|Hanging from a towel makes you close your hand much harder than on the bar.|Loop one or two towels over the bar and grab an end in each hand. Hang with your arms straight and hold for the set time without easing off your grip.
Farmers hold|It's the stationary version of the farmer's carry: hold the weight standing with your shoulders back.|Grab a heavy dumbbell in each hand and stand up with your back straight and your arms straight. Hold the position without moving for the set time, with your shoulders down and your abs tight.
Colgado a una mano|Switch hands when you feel your grip starting to open.|Hang from the bar with one hand, with the other at your side or holding your wrist. Keep your shoulder active so you don't swing and hold for the set time before switching.
Russian twist|Rotate from your ribs, not just with your arms: your chest follows your hands.|Sit with your knees bent, lean your torso back with your back straight, and lift your feet off the floor if you can. Rotate your torso from side to side, bringing your hands together to each side.
Leñador en polea|Rotate your torso from the hips, bringing the cable diagonally from high to low, with your arms almost straight.|Set the pulley high and hold the handle with both hands at one side. Pull diagonally toward the opposite hip, rotating your torso and pivoting your back foot, and return slowly.
Toques de talón|Lift your shoulders off the floor and move your torso from side to side to touch each heel.|Lie on your back with your knees bent and your feet flat. Lift your shoulders off the floor and bend your torso to one side until your hand touches your heel, alternating sides.
Leñador en polea bajo|Low to high on the diagonal: bring the cable from your knee to above the opposite shoulder.|Set the pulley low and hold the handle with both hands next to your outside knee. Pull diagonally upward, rotating your torso, until your hands are above the opposite shoulder, and return slowly.
Rotación con mancuerna|Hold the dumbbell with your arms straight in front of your chest and rotate slowly to each side.|Standing or seated, hold a dumbbell with both hands in front of your chest. Rotate your torso to one side, keeping your hips still, return to the center, and rotate to the other side.
Rotación en máquina|Set the machine so the rotation comes from your torso and not your hips.|Sit in the rotation machine with your legs secured and your chest against the pad. Rotate your torso to one side against the resistance and return slowly; do your reps on both sides.
Russian twist con peso|Hold the weight close to your chest and touch the floor with it on each side without rounding your back.|Seated with your torso leaning back and a plate or a ball in your hands, rotate to one side until the weight almost touches the floor and repeat to the other side.
Giro de tronco con barra|With an unloaded bar on your shoulders, rotate slowly: it's a mobility exercise, not a strength one.|Standing with a light bar or a stick across your shoulders, rotate your torso from side to side under control, keeping your hips facing forward.
Abducción en máquina|Sit with your back straight and open your legs without rocking: the pause with your legs apart is what counts.|Sit in the abductor machine with the pads on the outside of your knees. Open your legs as far as you can, hold for a second, and close them slowly without letting the plates touch.
Abducción en polea|Standing sideways to the low pulley, move the far leg outward without leaning your torso.|Attach an ankle strap to the low pulley and stand sideways with the far ankle hooked up. Hold on to the frame and move your leg out, away from your body, as far as you can control; return slowly.
Abducción con banda|With the mini band at your knees, seated or lying down, open your legs against the resistance.|Sit or lie on your side with a mini band above your knees. Push your knees apart against the band, hold for a second, and bring them back together slowly.
Abducción tumbado de lado|Raise the top leg slightly back, leading with your heel: that's how the gluteus medius works.|Lie on your side with your legs straight and stacked. Raise the top leg about 30-40 cm with your foot pointing forward and lower it slowly.
Zancada atrás|Stepping back is easier on the front knee and works the glutes more.|Standing with a dumbbell in each hand, take a long step back and lower your back knee until it almost touches the floor. Push through the heel of the front leg to return to the start, and alternate.
Zancada atrás en Smith|The guide rails give you stability: focus on pushing through the heel of the front leg.|With the Smith bar on your back, take a long step back and lower your back knee toward the floor. Come up by pushing with the front leg and finish one side before switching.
Zancada atrás con déficit|With your front foot on a plate, the glutes work through a longer range.|Place your front foot on a plate or a low step and take a long step back with the other leg. Lower your back knee below the level of the step and come back by pushing through the front heel.
Step up alto|With a high box the hips work more: lean your torso forward a little as you step up.|Put one foot on a box above knee height. Lean your torso slightly, push through the top heel until the leg is straight, and lower the other foot slowly to the floor.
Sentadilla búlgara con énfasis en glúteo|Lean your torso forward and move your front foot away from the bench: that way the glutes stretch more.|Rest the top of your back foot on a bench and step the other leg a long step forward. With your torso leaning forward, lower until you feel the stretch in your glute and come up by pushing through the front heel.
Handstand push-up|Form a triangle with your head and hands on the floor, and use a leg kip only if you've mastered it.|Kick up into a handstand with your feet against the wall and your hands slightly wider than your shoulders. Lower your head to the floor or the mat by bending your elbows and press until your arms are straight, using a leg kip if the WOD allows it.
Ring dips|Turn your palms out at the top and squeeze the rings against your body so they don't drift apart.|Support yourself on the rings with your arms straight and the rings close to your body. Lower by bending your elbows until your shoulders are below your elbows and press until your arms are straight, turning your palms out at the end.
Wall walk|Walk your hands toward the wall while your feet climb it, until your chest almost touches it.|Lie face down with your feet touching the wall. Push up into the push-up position, walk your feet up the wall, and walk your hands back until your chest almost touches it; walk back out until you're lying down.
Pino contra la pared|Push the floor away with your arms straight and squeeze your abs so you don't arch your back.|Stand facing the wall or facing away from it and kick up into a handstand with your hands a hand's width from it. Keep your arms straight, your body straight, and your glutes squeezed for the set time.
Handstand push-up estricto|No leg drive: lower your head to the floor slowly and press with your shoulders and triceps only.|In a handstand against the wall, with your hands slightly wider than your shoulders, lower your head until it touches the floor under control. Press until your arms are straight without moving your legs or taking them off the wall.
Parallette push-ups|The parallettes let your chest go below your hands: use the extra range.|Put your hands on two low parallettes and your feet on the floor, with your body straight. Lower your chest between the parallettes below hand level and press until your arms are straight.
Pike push-ups|With your hips high and your body in an inverted V, your head comes down in front of your hands: it works the shoulders.|Put your hands and feet on the floor and lift your hips to form an inverted V. Bend your elbows, lowering your head toward the floor in front of your hands, and press to come back up.
Carrera 1 km|It's the stretch that repeats eight times in Hyrox: learn your cruising pace and don't change it coming out of each station.|Run 1 km at your target pace with a short stride and a high cadence, without speeding up at the start. If you do it within a station workout, come out of each one at the same running pace.
Carrera 1 km con chaleco|The vest changes your footstrike: shorten your stride and land under your hips.|Put on a weighted vest snug to your torso and run 1 km at a steady pace, slower than without weight. Keep your torso upright and your shoulders relaxed.
Carrera 1 km ritmo Hyrox|Run at the exact pace you want to hold in competition so your body memorizes it.|Work out your Hyrox pace per kilometer and run 1 km nailing it, checking your watch every 200-250 m. Use it between stations in your simulation workouts.
Carrera 800 m tras estación|Your legs come out of the station heavy: give them the first 200 m to loosen up.|As soon as you finish a station, like wall balls or the sled, head out for an 800 m run. Start a little easier and reach your running pace around the middle of the stretch.
Comba|Jump just high enough for the rope to pass and spin it with your wrists, elbows close to your body.|Hold the rope with your elbows at your sides and jump with your feet together or alternating, bouncing on the balls of your feet. One turn of the rope per jump, at a steady rhythm, until you complete the set time or jumps.
Natación|Breathe every two or three strokes and keep your body in line with the surface of the water.|Swim for the set time or distance in the stroke you're best at, at a steady pace. In freestyle, rotate your body with each stroke to breathe without lifting your head.
Caminata inclinada|Walk uphill with your torso upright and without holding on: it's low-impact cardio that burns much more than on the flat.|Find a hill or set the treadmill to a 10-12% incline and walk at a brisk pace, 4.5 to 6 km/h, for the set time. Keep your torso straight and swing your arms without leaning on the rails: if you need to hold on, slow down.
Comba por intervalos|Alternate 30-60 seconds of fast jumping with rest: the pace of the interval should be high.|Jump rope at a hard pace for the set interval and rest for the same time or less. Repeat for the set number of rounds, trying not to trip on any of them.
Caminata rápida|Walk as if you were running late: your breathing should feel faster, but you should still be able to talk.|Walk at a brisk pace for the set time, with natural strides and your arms swinging in rhythm. Choose flat terrain or gentle climbs.
Senderismo|Fit the backpack to your hips and use poles on the descents to look after your knees.|Hike at a steady pace for the set time or distance, with proper footwear and water. On the climbs, shorten your step; on the descents, bend your knees slightly.
Natación intervalos|Swim short reps at a hard pace and rest at the wall just long enough to repeat the same time.|Swim reps of 50 to 200 m at an intense pace with a short rest at the wall between them. Repeat for the set number of reps, holding your stroke technique.
Saco de boxeo|Hit with the hip turn and not just the arm, and always protect your face with the other hand.|With gloves and wraps on, stand in front of the bag in your guard. Throw combinations of straights, hooks, and uppercuts for the set rounds, moving around the bag and resting between rounds.
Comba boxeo|Jump with a bounce, alternating feet, like boxers do, and keep the rope low.|With the rope, jump alternating feet with a small bounce on each side, as if jogging in place. Keep your shoulders relaxed and hold the rhythm for the set rounds.
Curl en máquina|Line up your elbow with the machine's pivot: if they don't match, the movement feels off.|Adjust the seat so your elbows are over the machine's pivot with your arms supported. Curl the handles by bending your elbows, squeeze, and return slowly without dropping the weight.
Curl en máquina unilateral|Work one arm and then the other: it's the easiest way to even them out.|On the curl machine, grab the handle with one hand with your arm supported. Bend your elbow to the end of the range, return slowly, and switch arms when the set is done.
Curl de muñeca inverso|With your palms down, the extensors do the work: use light weight and a full range.|Seated with your forearms on your thighs and your palms down, hold the bar with your wrists past your knees. Raise the backs of your hands as far as possible and lower slowly.
Curl de muñeca inverso con mancuerna|A light dumbbell is enough: the wrist extensors are small muscles.|Rest one forearm on your thigh or a bench with your palm down and a light dumbbell in your hand. Raise the back of your hand and lower it slowly; switch arms when you finish.
Extensión de muñeca en polea|The low pulley keeps tension on the wrist extensors through the whole range.|Facing a low pulley with a short bar, rest your forearms on a bench with your palms down. Raise your hands by extending your wrists and lower them slowly.
Extensión de tríceps en máquina|Adjust the seat so your elbows line up with the pivot and push until your arms are fully straight.|Sit in the machine with your back supported and your elbows on the pad, in line with the pivot. Push the handles by extending your elbows, squeeze your triceps, and return slowly to 90°.
Fondos en máquina sentado|Seated, the movement is like a dip but without carrying your body weight: push down with your elbows tucked in.|Sit in the dip machine with your back supported and grab the handles at your sides. Push down until your arms are straight with your elbows close to your body and return slowly.
Vacuum abdominal|Blow out all your air and draw your belly button toward your spine without breathing for a few seconds.|Standing, on all fours, or lying down, empty your lungs and draw your belly button in and up as far as possible. Hold the contraction for 10 to 20 seconds and breathe normally before repeating.
Hollow hold con balón|Hold the ball between your feet or in your hands: the extra weight lengthens the lever.|Lie on your back in the hollow position, with your lower back pressed into the floor, holding a ball with your arms straight overhead or between your feet. Hold the position for the set time.
Aducción en máquina|Close your legs and don't bounce as you open them: the adductor stretch should feel comfortable.|Sit in the adductor machine with the pads on the inside of your knees. Bring your legs together, squeezing, hold for a second, and open them slowly until you feel a gentle stretch.
Aducción en polea|Standing sideways to the pulley, cross the near leg in front of the other one.|Attach an ankle strap to the low pulley and stand sideways with the near ankle hooked up. Move that leg inward, crossing it in front of the standing leg, and return slowly.
Aducción con balón|Squeeze the ball between your knees for a few seconds: it's adductor work with no machine.|Lie on your back or sit with your knees bent and a ball between them. Squeeze it hard for 5-10 seconds, relax, and repeat.
Elevación de puntas (tibial)|Lean your back against the wall with your heels forward and pull your toes up toward your shins.|Standing with your back against the wall and your heels a foot away from it, raise your toes toward your shins as far as possible and lower them slowly without letting them rest fully on the floor.
Tibial en máquina|Put the tops of your feet under the pad and pull your toes toward you with your heels down.|Sit in the tibialis machine with your heels supported and the tops of your feet under the pad. Pull your toes toward your shins against the resistance and lower them slowly.
Tibial con banda|Tie the band to something fixed in front of you and loop it over the top of your foot.|Seated on the floor with your legs straight, loop the band over the top of your foot and anchor it in front of you. Pull your toes toward you against the resistance and return slowly; switch feet.
`);
